hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17035","(17035) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: It is not appropriate for a man to collect Between a woman and her breastfeeding paternal aunt from among the possessions of the right hand."
"17036","(17036) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the day of the conquest of Mecca: A woman shall not be married to her paternal aunt or maternal aunt.\n(Ahmad 2/207 Abd al-Razzaq 10751)"
"17037","(17037) Kathir bin Hisham narrated to us, Ja’far bin Burqan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, he said: He forbade. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said that a woman should be married off to her paternal aunt or to her maternal aunt."
"17038","(17038) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Husayn al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Amr ibn Shu’ayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that a man He married a woman to her maternal aunt, but Omar attacked him and separated them."
"17039","(17039) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ma’qil, on the authority of Ata’ and Yazid bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Hasan. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace, that a woman may be married to her paternal aunt or paternal aunt."
"17040","(17040) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It is disliked to bring together two cousins. Because of corruption between them."
"17041","(17041) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, that Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad told him that a son of Ali brought together two of his cousins’ daughters. He said: So they entered upon him during the night."
"17042","(17042) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he was reluctant to bring together relatives from For the sake of estrangement."
"17043","(17043) Zayd ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd, who said: He was asked: Will he make peace? Is it permissible for a woman to marry her paternal uncle? He said: This is the severance and the severance is not valid."
"17044","(17044) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, Khalid Al-Fafa narrated to me, on the authority of Issa bin Talhi, who said: The Messenger of God forbade May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that a woman be married to her relatives for fear of estrangement. (Abu Dawud 208 and Abd al-Razzaq 10767)"
"17045","(17045) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Abi Zayd, on the authority of his father, that Siba’ ibn Thabit married His son, Rabah bin Wahb, had a son from someone else, and she had a son from someone else. So the boy blew up at the slave girl and appeared. He carried the slave girl and took them to Omar ibn al-Khattab. He confessed, flogged them, and was keen to bring them together, but the boy refused."
"17046","(17046) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, about a man and a woman. Each one of them had done something bad to the other and then wanted to marry her. He said: There is no problem, the beginning of it is fornication and the end of it is marriage."
"17047","(17047) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Its beginning is fornication and its end is marriage."
"17048","(17048) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Janab, on the authority of Bukair ibn al-Akhnas, on the authority of his father, who said: I recited from the night (Ham Asq) So I passed by these verses: {And it is He who accepts repentance from His servants and pardons evil deeds, and He knows what you do} So I went to Abdullah to ask him about her, and a man came to him and asked him about a man who commits adultery with a woman and then marries her. So Abdullah recited: {And it is He who accepts repentance from His servants and pardons sins}"
"17049","(17049) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Urwa bin Abdullah bin Qushayr, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Its beginning is incest and its end is sexual intercourse, or its beginning is forbidden and its end is lawful."
"17050","(17050) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; That a man committed adultery with a woman while they were virgins, so Abu Bakr flogged them and banished them, then married them to him after a year."
"17051","(17051) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: There is no harm in him marrying her."
"17052","(17052) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, who said: A man asked him about a man who committed suicide. With a woman, will he marry her? He said: Yes, and he recited these verses: {And it is He who accepts repentance from His servants and pardons sins}"
"17053","(17053) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Shayba Abi Na’am, who said: Sa’id bin Jubayr was asked, while I was listening, about a man who committed suicide. With a woman, will he marry her? He said: The beginning of it is incest and the end of it is marriage. His wealth is permissible for him."
"17054","(17054) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd, who said: He was asked about a man who commits adultery in a mirror and then He marries her, he said: He has more right to her, but he ruined her."
"17055","(17055) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar ibn al-Walid, on the authority of Ikrim, who said: There is no problem, there is a man in his house who stole a palm tree. Then he bought it."
"17056","(17056) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Hassan, who said: I heard Hanzalah say: I asked Salim about him, and he said: There is no problem. With it"
"17057","(17057) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: If they repent and make amends, there is no problem. With it"
"17058","(17058) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Mansour, or Ibn Mansour, on the authority of Salah bin Ashim said: There is no problem if they are repentant, then God is more deserving of their repentance, but if they were adulterers, then the evil is upon them. The evil one."
"17059","(17059) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, who said: I have heard that Omar bin Abdul-Aziz was asked about a woman who was afflicted with A sin, then it was seen that she was better. Should the man marry her? Then Omar said to him, as he had told me: Do you think I will forbid you?"
"17060","(17060) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abi Yazeed, who said: Ibn Abbas was asked about a man who committed adultery. With a woman and he wanted to marry her, he said: Now he has done what is permissible."
"17061","(17061) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid and Ata’, who said: If a man commits adultery with a woman It is permissible for him."
"17062","(17062) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, his leaders narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab, Jabir bin Abdullah, and Sa’id bin A tyrant in a man who commits sexual intercourse with a woman and then marries her. They said: There is no harm in that as long as they repent and make amends."
"17063","(17063) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, regarding a man who commits suicide. With a woman and then he marries her. He said: The beginning of it was incest and the end of it was marriage. The beginning of it was forbidden and the end of it was lawful."
"17064","(17064) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Marwan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Sada’i, on the authority of Ali, who said: A man came to him, He said: I have a cousin who has fallen in love with her, and I have had sexual intercourse with her. He said: If it is something esoteric, meaning intercourse, then no. If it is something apparent, meaning the direction of the direction, then there is no problem."
"17065","(17065) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah. He said: No. They are still adulterers."
"17066","(17066) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Aisha said: They will continue to be fornicators as long as they are together."
"17067","(17067) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid that he said: They did not commit adultery. To make between him and her the sea."
"17068","(17068) Asbat narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu al-Jahm, on the authority of the innocent in a man who commits immoral acts with a woman and then He marries her. He said: They will never cease to be fornicators."
"17069","(17069) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Issa bin Hattan, on the authority of Muslim bin Salam, on the authority of Ali bin Talq, who said: I heard the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, says: God is not ashamed of the truth, do not approach women in their infirmities, or he said: in Adbarhanna (Tirmidhi 1166. Dharmi 1141)"
"17070","(17070) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Uthman, on the authority of Makhramam bin Sulayman, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God does not look at a man who has intercourse with a man or a woman in her anus.\n(Tirmidhi 1165. Ibn Hibban 4418)"
"17071","(17071) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade women to be intercourse with He marveled at them and said: God is not ashamed of the truth."
"17072","(17072) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: Sodomy minor. (Nasa’i 8997)"
"17073","(17073) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Uqba ibn Wasaj, he said: Abu al-Darda’ said: Woe. Only an unbeliever does that."
"17074","(17074) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Uqba bin Wasaj, on the authority of Abu al-Darda`, who said: Who will do that except An infidel"
"17075","(17075) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Shaqri, on the authority of Abu Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, who said: It is forbidden for you to have sex with women."
"17076","(17076) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Layth, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: Whoever comes to him, whether men or women, has Infidelity"
"17077","(17077) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Hakim Al-Athram, on the authority of Abu Tamimah Al-Hujamiyy, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: Whoever has intercourse with a menstruating woman, or an anterior woman, has disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad. May God bless him and grant him peace.\n(Abu Dawud 3899, Darami 1136)"
"17078","(17078) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Kathir, who said: Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah bin Al-Husayn narrated to us Al-Khattimi, on the authority of Abd Al-Malik bin Qais Al-Khattami, on the authority of Harami bin Abdullah, who said: I heard Khuzaymah bin Thabit He says: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: God is not ashamed of the truth, do not approach women in their miracles.\n(Tabarani 3740, Bayhaqi 196)"
"17079","(17079) Ahmad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Wahib, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Mukhlid, on the authority of Abu Hariri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God does not look at a man who has intercourse with a woman in her anus.\n(Abu Dawud 2155. Ibn Majah 1923)"
"17080","(17080) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Al-Salt bin Bahram narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman bin Masoud narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Mu’tamir. Or Abu Al-Juwayriyah said: He called Ali from the pulpit and said: Ask me, ask me, and a man said: Should women be given access to What do you think? He said: You have revolted, may God revere you. Have you not seen that God Almighty says: “Do you commit the indecency?”"
"17081","(17081) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: She was one of us if she was A menstruating woman was commanded by the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to wrap herself in a garment, then he would go out to her. (Bukhari 3000, Muslim 242)"
"17082","(17082) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha She said: When one of us was menstruating, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded her to cover herself immediately after her menstruation, and then He engages in it, and which of you is the owner of its land, just as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was the owner of its land. (Bukhari 3020 Muslim 2)"
"17083","(17083) Abbad bin Awwam and Ali bin Mushir told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, who said: You informed me. Maimunah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of the Prophet, in a similar way. (Bukhari 303. Ahmad 6/336)"
"17084","(17084) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Abdī, that Umm Salamah said: I died while I was with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, means: I had my period in my bed, so I went to stay late, and he said: Where you are, it was enough for me to make it on you. A dress.\n(Tabarani 11602)"
"17085","(17085) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Umm Salamah regarding intercourse with a menstruating woman: if he was on her private parts. rags"
"17086","(17086) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Ali, who said: What is above the garment."
"17087","(17087) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: What Above the garment."
"17088","(17088) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid, he said: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr saying: You have what is above the garment, but do not see what is above it. Under it"
"17089","(17089) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Maymun ibn Mihran, on the authority of Aisha, that she was asked: What does a man have? Is your woman menstruating? She said: What is above the garment?"
"17090","(17090) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If she throws a rag on her private parts, he should be intimate with her."
"17091","(17091) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, who said: If a menstruating woman refrains from harming her, then do something to her. You wish"
"17092","(17092) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: He will come to her as long as the blood has missed."
"17093","(17093) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mas’ar ibn Habib al-Jarmiy, who said: I asked Abu Qalābī: What kind of wife does a man have? Is she menstruating? He said: They mention what is above the garment."
"17094","(17094) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Salt ibn Bāram, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: You have what is above the garment."
"17095","(17095) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Makin, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: What is above the garment."
"17096","(17096) Hatem bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala that he heard a man asking Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, He said: Should I have intercourse with my wife while she is menstruating? He said: Put a piece of clothing between you and that, then have sex with her."
"17097","(17097) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ghaylan, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: There is no harm in him placing it on the private parts, but not He enters it."
"17098","(17098) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of Shayba bin Hisham Al-Rasibiy, who said: I asked Salim, On the authority of a man who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating, and he said: As for us, the family of Umar, we will isolate her from her."
"17099","(17099) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: What is above the garment."
"17100","(17100) Asbat narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ubaidah, regarding a menstruating woman: You have what is above the garment."
"17101","(17101) Shababi told us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Habib, the client of Urwa, on the authority of Nadba Mawla Maimouna, on the authority of Maimouna, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He used to have intercourse with any of his wives while she was menstruating if she was wearing an garment that reached halfway up the thighs, or The knees are pressed against it.\n(Abu Dawud 271, Ahmad 6/336)"
"17102","(17102) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in playing on her stomach and between her thighs."
"17103","(17103) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Asim bin Amr Al-Bajli, who said: Some people from Iraq went out, and when they came Ali Omar said to them: Who are you from? They said: From the people of Iraq. He said: By permission did you come? They said, yes, so they asked him about what is permissible for a man to have sex with his menstruating wife, and he said: you asked me about the qualities he asked me about. One after I asked the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: As for what a man has of his menstruating wife, he has something above The loincloth"
"17104","(17104) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He says: I am in you. He is willing, and I want a woman whose affairs are such and such, and he presents it to her by saying."
"17105","(17105) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, in his saying: {And there is no blame on you for what you expose yourself to. Whoever proposes to women} He said: He says: You are beautiful, and indeed you are a hypocrite. Indeed, you are for good. And he hates it for him to say: Do not miss me. By yourself, and I am anxious for you."
"17106","(17106) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he saw no harm in all of that."
"17107","(17107) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It was disliked for him to say: When her waiting period has ended, I will marry you. And he says whatever he wants."
"17108","(17108) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He says: I admire you and I desire you, but I do not Let us lose your soul."
"17109","(17109) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: He says: Indeed, you are beautiful, and indeed you are hypocritical, and indeed you are Good"
"17110","(17110) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of The woman's husband dies, and the man wants to propose to her and talk to her. He said: He says: I admire you, and I admire you. I am eager for you, and I am anxious for you, and the like."
"17111","(17111) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ubaydah, regarding his saying: {And It is a sin upon you regarding what you presented of his speeches to women. He said: mention her to her guardian, but do not make her aware."
"17112","(17112) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said To Fatima bint Qays: Go to Umm Sharik and do not escape from us yourself. (Muslim 39. Abu Dawud 2281)"
"17113","(17113) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr {Unless you say a word. Kindly} He said: He says: Indeed, I desire you, and I hope that God will bring you and me together."
"17114","(17114) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: He says: Indeed, you are beautiful and indeed you are a hypocrite, even if God has decreed a matter that happened."
"17115","(17115) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in the gift of marriage in the case of marriage."
"17116","(17116) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Fatima: Do not miss us yourself."
"17117","(17117) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: {And there is no blame on you for what you expose. He said: A man turns away and says: I want to get married, and he does not use the accusative case in his engagements."
"17118","(17118) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Ammar bin Ruzaq, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, in his saying: {And there is no blame on you for what you address to women} He said: He says, Indeed, He is willing in you. I wish I had married you so that they would know that he wants to marry her other than it being obligatory under his contract, or He made a covenant with her."
"17119","(17119) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, he said: Recite This verse: {And there is no blame on you for that which you expose to women}. He said: He says regarding the waiting period: Indeed, it is upon you. I am eager, and I am willing for you, and so on."
"17120","(17120) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir: {And there is no blame on you for what you presented of his speeches. An-Nisa’} He said: He says: Indeed, you are beautiful and you are hypocritical, and if God has decreed anything, it will happen."
"17121","(17121) Shababah narrated to us, on the authority of Warqa’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid: {In what you presented with him of his sermons. An-Nisa’” said: A man’s saying to a woman: “You are beautiful, and indeed you are hypocritical, and you are indeed good.” And let it be a remembrance. He proposed to her in his own right, he did not do it to her, this is all a known solution."
"17122","(17122) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, regarding his saying: {Unless you say a well-known word} He said: He says: I long for you."
"17123","(17123) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Abdullah bin Qays, that a servant of Abu Musa, and he was the owner of his camels. He married a mother from Banu Ja`dah and brought five animals to her. He told Abu Musa, so he sent to them: Send to me my servant and my money. They said: As for the boy, he is your boy, and as for the money, it was permissible for him to please our friend. So they disputed with Othman bin Affan, and he decided for them. Othman gave him one-fifth of what was permissible for him to marry his companion, and he returned three-fifths to Abu Musa."
"17124","(17124) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: A slave of Abu Musa was married during the reign of ‘Ali. Five qayla'as. This was brought up to Omar, so he gave the woman two qayla'as and three qayla'as to Abu Musa, or he gave her three qayla'as. He responded to Abu Musa Qalusin, saying: I think he got married without his permission."
"17125","(17125) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama bin Tammam, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: There is no friendship for her. She permitted her private parts."
"17126","(17126) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Amir, who said: He will take from her what she has consumed, and what she has not It consumes you"
"17127","(17127) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He will take from her what she did not consume. As for what it consumes, nothing."
"17128","(17128) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, who said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a slave who marries a woman without permission. His master, he said: There will be separation between them and there will be no friendship with her. Whatever she took will be taken from her."
"17129","(17129) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; There is a Mamluk who got married without his master’s permission, so he consummated the marriage with her and told her what she had taken."
"17130","(17130) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri regarding a slave: If he marries without his master’s permission, it is not a marriage. And she has nothing."
"17131","(17131) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a slave who married without his master’s permission and gave a dowry, he said: If he consummated the marriage with her, then she gets the dowry, and if he did not consummate the marriage with her, he took it. The Lord is the Sadiq."
"17132","(17132) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I heard the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he says: Any slave who marries without the permission of his master is a prostitute. (Abu Dawud 2080, Ahmed 377)"
"17133","(17133) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, saying: Al-Qasim bin Abdul-Wahid narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Whichever slave gets married or says: He has intercourse Without the permission of his family, he is a prostitute. (Hakim 194. Ahmad 3/382)"
"17134","(17134) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Marrying a slave without permission His master committed adultery, and the one who married him will be punished."
"17135","(17135) Zayd bin Harun told us, saying: Sa’id bin Abi Aroub told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar. If his servant married without permission, the punishment would strike him."
"17136","(17136) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, he said: I asked Ghanim bin Qais, I said: The slave gets married. Without his master's permission, did he commit adultery? He said: He has disobeyed. I said: He has committed adultery? He said: He has disobeyed you."
"17137","(17137) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad about a slave who marries without the permission of his master, He said: He was about something and they asked about it."
"17138","(17138) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Ghayath, who said: A slave does not marry except with the permission of his master."
"17139","(17139) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, regarding his saying: {But do not date them secretly} He said: He does not take She had a covenant or covenant not to marry anyone else."
"17140","(17140) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, regarding his saying: {But do not date them secretly} He proposed to her during her waiting period."
"17141","(17141) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: {But do not date them secretly} He said: He meets the guardian and mentions them. Desire and eagerness."
"17142","(17142) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama bin Kail, on the authority of Muslim al-Batin, on the authority of Sa`id, who said: No. He is required to fulfill her waiting period by not marrying anyone else."
"17143","(17143) Shababah told us, on the authority of Warqa’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid: (But do not date them secretly) the man’s saying To the woman: Do not let yourself go away from me, for I will marry you. This is not permissible."
"17144","(17144) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Mukhlid, and Al-Hasan: {But do not date them secretly} They said: Adultery"
"17145","(17145) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Al-Hasan: {But do not date them secretly} He said: adultery."
"17146","(17146) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: I heard him say, “But do not date them secretly.” He said: Adultery"
"17147","(17147) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-Suddi, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Adultery."
"17148","(17148) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: Adultery."
"17149","(17149) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of Hayyan al-Araj, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd, who said: Adultery."
"17150","(17150) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Marthad, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: He does not judge her if he does not He married someone else."
"17151","(17151) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Hanash ibn Al-Mu’tamir, who said: A man was brought to Ali who had approved of himself. With adultery, Ali said to him: Have you been married? He said: Yes. He said: Then he will be stoned. He said: So he took him to prison, and when the evening came, he called for him and narrated his story to the people, and a man from the people said: Indeed. He had married a woman with whom he had not consummated the marriage, and he was happy about that for Ali, so the punishment struck him and separated him from his wife. And he gave her half of the dowry as he saw fit."
"17152","(17152) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir and on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan that the virgin if She committed adultery, was flogged, and there was separation between her and her husband, and she had nothing. Then Al-Hasan interpreted these verses: {And do not isolate yourself from them. That you may take away part of what you have given them, unless they bring something clearly indecent."
"17153","(17153) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There will be a separation between them and there will be no friendship between them."
"17154","(17154) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who marries a woman and then she commits adultery before consummating the sexual intercourse with her. He said: He will separate them, and there will be no friendship with her, and he will flog her. A hundred and a half years, and if he committed adultery, separate them."
"17155","(17155) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: This is his wife, and the punishment may be imposed upon him. If he so desires, he may be divorced. And if he wishes, he can keep him just as if he had broken the fast, his wife would not have been separated from him."
"17156","(17156) Gandar told us, on the authority of his people, about the ruling on a man who committed adultery before he had intercourse with his wife. His opinion is that there should be no separation between him and his wife."
"17157","(17157) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, about a man who married a woman and one of them committed an indecency before If he enters with her, he said: He will be flogged and not separated between them."
"17158","(17158) Ibn Fudail narrated to us on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Safiyya bint Abi Ubaid, who said: A man married One woman then committed adultery with another woman before consummating the sexual intercourse with his wife. Abu Bakr flogged him for a hundred and exiled him for a year."
"17159","(17159) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu al-Khalil, that Abu Alqamiya al-Hashemi narrated to us that Abu Saeed Al-Khudri told them: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent a group of secretaries on the day of Hunayn, and they struck a group of people alive. The Arabs on the Day of Awtas defeated them, killed them, and wounded women who had wives who had committed adultery. They were some of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. They sinned because of their deceit for the sake of their wives, so God revealed: {And chaste women, except those she possesses. Your oaths are lawful for you. (Muslim 33 Abu Dawud 2148)"
"17160","(17160) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Ali said, in the Almighty’s saying: {And the chaste women} He said: those who have wives from among the polytheists."
"17161","(17161) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, who said: Captive women had wives. Before they take you captive."
"17162","(1716) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Anas: {and chaste women} He said: Women with husbands."
"17163","(17163) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab. He said: Women with wives, this refers to Until God Almighty forbids adultery."
"17164","(17164) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ash’ath and Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Ubaidah: {And chaste women among the women} He said With his hand like this and he indicated the four: Except what your right hands possess."
"17165","(17165) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Salt, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Every married woman is forbidden to you, except for the captives you have captured."
"17166","(17166) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: It was revealed on the day of Awtas."
"17167","(17167) Ibn Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Hassan, who said: Every married woman is forbidden to you, except what your right hand possesses. It means from the captives."
"17168","(17168) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muhammad, like him."
"17169","(17169) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It is adultery, and Mujahid said: It is adultery, and Ikrimah said. : It is adultery {except what your oaths possess it} and Ibn Abbas said: {except what your oaths possess it} a man removing his child from a woman Abduh, and others said: The enemy’s captives will be brought home if our wives are taken captive."
"17170","(17170) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Four."
"17171","(17171) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: Four."
"17172","(1717) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah: {And chaste women, except those Your right hands are possessed. He said: married women."
"17173","(17173) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah, in his saying: {And chaste women} He said: Every married woman is forbidden to you, except what your right hand owns, or you buy."
"17174","(17174) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Every married woman is forbidden to you, except the one she owns. Your right hand is one of the captives, meaning {and chaste women}."
"17175","(17175) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, saying: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abd al-Karim, on the authority of Makhul: {And chaste women among the women} He said: Women with husbands."
"17176","(17176) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Mughal, on the authority of Abu Al-Sawda’, who said: I asked Ikrimah about her, and he said: No. I know, and I asked Al-Sha’abi, and he said: This is every woman who has a husband."
"17177","(17177) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: {And the chaste women} He said: Of all women, except those with wives who are captives."
"17178","(17178) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, in his saying: {And chaste women, except those your right hands possess} He said: Adultery, and Mujahid said: It is adultery, and Ibn Abbas said: It is adultery, except as long as your right hands possess it, such that a man takes away his daughter. His servant’s wife, so he may have intercourse with her if he wishes, and others said: Captives of the enemy."
"17179","(17179) Muhammad bin Al-Hasan narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Sa’id, in his saying: {And chaste women, except those “Your right hands possess” He said: It was revealed about the women of Hunayn’s family, when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, conquered Hunayn. The Muslims were captives, and when a man wanted to have sexual intercourse with one of their women, she would say: I have a husband, so they would go to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him. So mention that to him, so God Almighty revealed: {And the chaste women among the women, except those whom your right hands possess} He said: The captives. Of married women."
"17180","(17180) Shababah told us, on the authority of Warqa’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid: {And chaste women among the women} forbidding, about adultery."
"17181","(17181) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: Do not be deceived. This verse {except what your right hands possess} is only meant by it the female slaves and not the male servants."
"17182","(17182) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Razin, regarding his saying: {It is not permissible for you to marry women after that} He said: It is not permissible for you To you are polytheists, except those you take captive, or those your right hand possesses."
"17183","(17183) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: From a Muslim, a Christian, or an infidel."
"17184","(17184) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: {It is not permissible for you to have women again} He said: The women of the nations are from the People of the Book."
"17185","(17185) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ali bin Bathimah, who said: I heard Mujahid saying: {It is not permissible for you The women afterward} He said: after this reason."
"17186","(17186) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Dawud ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abi Musa, on the authority of Ziyad, who said: It was said to my father: If the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had perished, would it be permissible for him to marry? He said: Who will prevent him? God permitted him to have multiple wives, so he could marry whomever he wanted. Then he recited these verses: {O Prophet! We have made lawful for you your wives who are married} until the end of the verse. (Tabari 29. Dharmi 2240)"
"17187","(17187) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not die. And peace be upon him until women were made lawful to him. (Tirmidhi 3216. Ahmad 41)"
"17188","(17188) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’: {And do not exchange them for other wives, even if you like them. They are beautiful. He said: Do not exchange them for either Jewish or Christian women."
"17189","(17189) Yahya bin Abdul-Malik bin Abi Ghaniyya told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hakam. He said: From the people of The book, or Arabic."
"17190","(17190) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Al-Sadi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, in his saying: {And do not change them. Of wives} He said: That is, if he divorced them, it would not be permissible for him to replace them. He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He may have sex with whomever he wants after the revelation, and she descends, and there are nine wives under him, and he marries the mother of his beloved and his two maidens."
"17191","(17191) Affan told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Al-Hasan: {And do not change them by any number of wives} He said: May God limit it to his nine wives from whom he died. He said: Ali said: So I told that to Ali bin Hussein, and he said: Yes. He was allowed to get married."
"17192","(17192) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Shubarmah, on the authority of Ikrimah: (An adulterer does not marry anyone but an adulterer.) No. The adulterer commits adultery except for his own fornication."
"17193","(17193) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab: {The adulterer only has sex with An adulterer or a polytheist. He said: It was said: Its version is the one after it. It is said that it is one of the days of the Muslims."
"17194","(17194) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Ali bin Muslim, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, who said: He does not commit adultery except An adulterer, or an polytheist."
"17195","(17195) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I heard him say: Be Prostitution in pre-Islamic times"
"17196","(17196) Abdou bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of Asim bin Al-Mundhir, he said: I asked Urwah, about His saying: {The adulterer shall not marry except an adulterer or a polytheist} He said: They were promiscuous women of the pre-Islamic era who had women who saw them. They are known for it."
"17197","(17197) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Women who disdained themselves during the pre-Islamic era."
"17198","(17198) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Salama, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, regarding his saying: (An adulterer may only marry an adulterer or an polytheist.) And the adulterer shall not marry her except an adulterer or a polytheist.) He said: He does not commit adultery when She commits adultery except with an adulteress like her."
"17199","(17199) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Ya`la ibn Muslim, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, similar to him."
"17200","(17200) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Shu’bi, the client of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: For the purposes of the pre-Islamic era, they will place banners like the banners of the ancient kingdoms on their gates, and people will come to them. They are known for that."
"17201","(17201) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of Asim bin Al-Mundhir, on the authority of Urwah, something similar."
"17202","(17202) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Amr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas He said: {The adulterer shall not marry except an adulterer or a polytheist.} What he means by marriage is: he has intercourse with her."
"17203","(17203) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid bin Dinar, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: No. No one will have intercourse with her except an adulterer or a polytheist."
"17204","(17204) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sufyan al-Tamar al-Asfari, who said: I heard Sa`id bin Jubayr saying: Be prostitutes. In Mecca before Islam, there were men who would marry them and they would spend on them what they earned. When Islam came, they married them. Men from the people of Islam, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade that to them."
"17205","(17205) Affan told us, he said, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: (The adulterer does not marry anyone except an adulterer or a polytheist) He said: The adulterer does not commit adultery except with his fornicator or a polytheist, but God A nickname"
"17206","(17206) Shababah narrated to us, on the authority of Warqa’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, regarding his saying: (The adulterer does not marry anyone except Adulteress (adulteress) are prostitutes who were pre-Islamic, and it was said to them: This is forbidden, so they wanted to marry them, but God forbade them. May we marry you."
"17207","(17207) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Women are permissible for the fornicator to commit adultery. He said: And I asked Al-Hasan, He said: We do not issue fatwas regarding hidden matters, but a limited person can only marry a limited person."
"17208","(17208) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ibn Sabit, that Ali was brought to a certain extent and married a woman other than him. limited, so he separated them."
"17209","(17209) Bakkar bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of his brother Abdullah bin Ubaidah that A servant of Banu Harithah was flogged for adultery, and a man wanted to marry her. He consulted Abu Hurairah, and he said: No, unless You would have done the same as her work."
"17210","(17210) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qays ibn Muslim, on the authority of Tariq ibn Shihab, that a man wanted to marry A son, and she said: I am afraid to expose you. I have sinned. Omar came and said: Haven’t you repented? He said: Yes, he said: So marry her."
"17211","(17211) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha, that the wife of Rifa’ah Al-Qurazi She came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I was with Rifa’a al-Qurazi and he divorced me, so my divorce was finalized and I got married. Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Zubayr, but he had with him something like the hem of a garment, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, smiled and said: Do you want to return to your high status? Not until you taste his honey and he tastes yours. (Bukhari 2439. Muslim 111)"
"17212","(17212) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked. May God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is not permissible for him until the other tastes her sweetness and she tastes it. Her sweetheart. (Abu Dawud 2303. Ahmad 6/42)"
"17213","(17213) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Like the hadith of Al-A'mash. (Bukhari 5261, Muslim 115)"
"17214","(17214) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. In the same way\n(Bukhari 52651 Muslim 114)"
"17215","(17215) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Alqamiya ibn Marthad, on the authority of Sulayman ibn Razin, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He was asked The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of a man who divorced his wife three times and she married a husband other than him. He closed the door and let her go. Then he divorced her before consummating the sexual intercourse with her, saying: She is not permissible for him until she marries another husband and tastes her sweetness.\n Waki' said in the end: Razin bin Sulaiman. (Ahmad 2/25, Bayhaqi 375)"
"17216","(17216) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: Ali said: It is not permissible for him until he shakes him. Al-Bakr, he said: And Aisha said: Until the other tastes her sweetness and she tastes his sweetness."
"17217","(17217) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Yahya ibn Yazid al-Hinai, on the authority of Anas, who said: It is not permissible for the first person until The other person has intercourse with her and enters with her."
"17218","(17218) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abi Tahya, who said: Abu Hurairah said: It is not permissible for the first one until the other has intercourse with her."
"17219","(17219) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah: It is not permissible for him even He healed her with it, and Ali said: Until she tastes her sweetness."
"17220","(17220) Al-Ashib Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Al-Harith Al-Ghaffari, on the authority of Abu Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Until you taste its honey. (Ibn Jarir 477)"
"17221","(17221) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalaab, on the authority of Anas, who said: If a virgin man marries his wife, he stays She has seven, and if the married man gets married, he stays with her three. Khalid said: Abu Qalab said: But if I said: It is, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, but it is a Sunnah. Khaled said: I narrated it to Ibn Sirin, and he said: You have increased this by four. And this is the night.\n(Bukhari 5213, Muslim 1084)"
"17222","(17222) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalāb, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: For a virgin, seven, and for a married woman, three. (Dharmi 2009, Muslim 1084)"
"17223","(17223) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. (Dharmi 2009)"
"17224","(17224) Yahya bin Saeed told us on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Bakr bin Abd al-Rahman bin al-Harith bin Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, got married Umm Salama stayed with her for three days and said to her: There is no shame for you and your family. If you wish, I will give you seven days, and if you wish, I will give you seven days. To you I have obeyed my wives. (Muslim 1083. Abu Dawud 2115)"
"17225","(17225) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam. He said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married Umm Salamah He stayed with her for three days and said: If you wish, I will do seven for you, and if I do for you, I will do for someone else. It was said to Al-Hakam: Who told you this? Hadith? He said: This hadith is well known to the people of Hijaz."
"17226","(17226) Abdou bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of Ibrahim and Ash-Shu’bi, who said: If a virgin marries his wife, He stayed with her for seven days, and when a married man married his wife, he stayed with her for three days."
"17227","(17227) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, the same."
"17228","(17228) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Three nights for a virgin and two nights for a married man."
"17229","(17229) Abdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan. He said, “He stays with a virgin three times and for a married woman.” Two nights"
"17230","(17230) Abduh told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He stays with the firstborn three times and divides, and when He married the married man, stayed for two nights, then divided."
"17231","(17231) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he reported that he said: The virgin three and the married man. Two nights"
"17232","(17232) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Salamah ibn Wahram, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: For a virgin, seven And for the garment, three."
"17233","(17233) Abu Qattan told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, who said: They are both equal in oath."
"17234","(17234) Abdul-Wahhab bin Ata’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab and Khalas. They said: If a virgin marries his wife, he stays with her for three nights and then divides his share, and if he marries a virgin, he stays with her for two nights and then He swears"
"17235","(17235) Yazeed told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, who said: It is Sunnah for a virgin to give seven and for a married man three. Humayd said: Al-Hasan said: Seven and two nights."
"17236","(17236) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ghaylan bin Jami’, on the authority of Abd al-Malik al-Zarrad, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Qumair, On the authority of Aisha, who said: The woman undergoing menstruation should not have intercourse with her husband."
"17237","(17237) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, did he dislike having intercourse with them? Her husband"
"17238","(17238) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, that he used to hate it for a man to have intercourse with his wife. It is mustahaadah."
"17239","(17239) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of the ruling. He said: She should not have sexual intercourse, nor should she fast."
"17240","(17240) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, who said: Al-Shu’abi said: Do not fast or Her husband cheated on her."
"17241","(17241) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, who said: I said to Suleiman bin Yassar: Should her husband come to her? He said: We do not say anything about it except what we heard."
"17242","(17242) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: The woman undergoing menstruation has intercourse with her husband."
"17243","(17243) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah, who said: I was informed that Al-Hajjaj said: If She doubted her menstruation. She washed and prayed, but do not bring it near until she is cleansed. He said: What a miserable thing he said. Prayer is the greatest sanctity."
"17244","(17244) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali, who said: Her husband came to her."
"17245","(17245) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Her husband had intercourse with her."
"17246","(17246) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Her husband can cheat on her if he wants."
"17247","(17247) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad regarding al-Mustadha: Her husband comes to her and she fasts."
"17248","(17248) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, in the matter of istihaadah, he said: He will come to her, the prayer is greater. Forbidden"
"17249","(17249) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, and al-Hasan in al-Mustadhadha: You fast and pray. She performs the rituals and her husband cheats on her."
"17250","(17250) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The woman who is mustahaadah fasts and prays. And her husband came to her."
"17251","(17251) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar ibn Musa, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, who said: The woman who undergoes menstruation must have intercourse with her husband."
"17252","(17252) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: Shurayh said: He is the husband, meaning {the one who In His Hand is the marriage contract}"
"17253","(17253) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Mulkiyah, he said: Sa`id ibn Jubayr: {the one in whose hand is the marriage contract} is the husband."
"17254","(17254) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, who said: Mujahid said: {The one in whose hand is the marriage contract} is the husband. {Unless they pardon} the woman returns her share {or the one in whose hand is pardoning the marriage contract} is the husband completing the entire dowry."
"17255","(17255) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Shurayh, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Shuraih and Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, they said: He is the husband."
"17256","(17256) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab: {Unless they pardon or pardon He in whose hand is the marriage contract} He said: He in whose hand is the marriage contract is the husband. If you wish to pardon him, then do not take from He befriended her for a reason, and if he wanted to, it would be halves between them."
"17257","(17257) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, that Nafi’ ibn Jubayr divorced his wife before he had intercourse with her, so he completed He gave her friendship and said: I am more deserving of pardon."
"17258","(17258) Zayd ibn Hubab told us, on the authority of Aflah ibn Sa’id, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ka’b say: “In whose hand is my necklace.” Marriage} means a husband, who gives freely what he has."
"17259","(17259) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: {In whose hand is the marriage contract} the husband, and as for his saying: {Unless they pardon, or they pardon, the one in whose hand is the marriage contract} So a woman is divorced by her husband before they consummate the marriage. Either she pardons half to her husband, or her husband pardons her and the dowry is completed for her."
"17260","(17260) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: He is the husband."
"17261","(17261) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, who said: He is the husband."
"17262","(17262) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Tawoos and Mujahid, who said: {By the One in Whose Hand is The marriage contract} is the guardian, and Sa`id bin Jubayr said: It is the husband. So they spoke to him about that, and they continued until they continued. Happy"
"17263","(17263) Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Saeed, who said: He is the husband."
"17264","(17244) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Ammar bin Abi Ammar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: {In whose hand is the marriage contract} the husband."
"17265","(17265) Ibn al-Darawardi told us, on the authority of Umar Mawla Ghufari, that Muhammad ibn Ka’b used to say: “It is in His hand that Marriage contract {husband}"
"17266","(17266) Ibn Aliyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Jarir ibn Hazim, on the authority of Issa ibn Asim, on the authority of Ali, who said: The husband.\n(Bayhaqi 251. Tabari 237)"
"17267","(17267) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: He is the husband."
"17268","(17268) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: He is the husband."
"17269","(17269) Marwan told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: He is the husband."
"17270","(17270) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid: {Unless they pardon or pardon Him in whose hand is The marriage contract} He said: the husband."
"17271","(17271) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr and Mujahid. They said: {Who In his hand is the marriage contract} the husband."
"17272","(17272) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He is the guardian."
"17273","(17273) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abu Raja’, who said: Al-Hasan was asked about “the one in whose hand is the marriage contract” and he said: The guardian"
"17274","(17274) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah. He said: He is the guardian."
"17275","(17275) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ikrim, who said: He is the guardian."
"17276","(17276) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim. He said, “He is the guardian.”"
"17277","(17277) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The one in whose hand is the father’s marriage contract."
"17278","(17278) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He is the guardian."
"17279","(17279) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Al-Zuhri {unless they pardon} He said: the Thaybatah {or they pardon In whose hand is the marriage contract} Wali al-Bakr."
"17280","(17280) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: God is pleased with pardoning and has commanded it, so if she pardons, then pardon, but if she refuses and her guardian pardons, then it is permissible, but if she refuses, then it is permissible."
"17281","(17281) Ziyad bin Al-Rabi’ narrated to us, on the authority of Salih Al-Dahdan, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: {And they do not Your adornment} He said: the palm and the face."
"17282","(17282) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah: {And they will not Their adornment, except what is apparent of it. He said: clothing."
"17283","(17283) Hafs told us, on the authority of Imran bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Abu Salih and Ikrimah: {And let them not display their adornments} They said: Kohl, ring, and clothes."
"17284","(17284) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abraham, From us"
"17285","(17285) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Alqamah ibn Marthad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The clothes."
"17286","(17286) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi. He said, kohl and clothing."
"17287","(17287) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Umm Shabib, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The heart and its thighs."
"17288","(17288) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Mahan: except what appears of it. He said: the garment."
"17289","(17289) Mu’tamar told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The face and the clothes."
"17290","(17290) Shababah ibn Siwar narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn al-Ghaz narrated to us, saying: Nafi’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Al-Zaynah. The outward appearance: the face and the palm of your hand."
"17291","(17291) Shabab bin Siwar narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Al-Ghaz narrated to us, saying: I heard Ata’ saying: The apparent adornment: Pigment and kohl."
"17292","(17292) Shababa told us, on the authority of Hisham, who said: I heard an alcoholic saying: The apparent adornment: the face and the palms."
"17293","(17293) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, who said: The clothes."
"17294","(17294) Affan narrated to us, saying: Sa’id bin Zaid narrated to us, saying: Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr: {And no They display their adornment except what is apparent of it.} The ring, the dye, and the kohl."
"17295","(17295) Affan told us, he said: Saeed bin Zaid told us, he said: Laith told us, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: pigment and kohl."
"17296","(17296) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Al-Zaynah Two adornments: an apparent adornment and an inward adornment that no one can see except the husband. As for the apparent adornment, it is the clothing. The hidden adornments include kohl, bracelet, and ring."
"17297","(17297) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: Their adornment, except what is apparent of it. He said: its face and its sufficiency."
"17298","(17298) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, who said: Enough. And her face."
"17299","(17299) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Salama bin Sabur narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul-Warith: {And let them not display their adornments except Whatever appears of it. He said: the palm and the ring."
"17300","(17300) Ahmad bin Bashir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Shubrumah, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: {Whatever appears of it} He said: The face And its gap is the river."
"17301","(17301) Abdā narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu al-Khalil, on the authority of Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, On the authority of Umm al-Fadl, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The breastfeeding and the two sucklings, the one who suckles and the two sucklings are not forbidden.\n(Muslim 18 Ahmad 6/339)"
"17302","(17302) Abdou and Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn al-Zubayr, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Do not forbid one sucking or one sucking. (Ibn Hibban 4225. Ahmad 4/4)"
"17303","(17303) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Ash-Sha’tha’i, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Breastfeeding is a form of famine. (Bukhari 5102, Muslim 32)"
"17304","(17304) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of al-Mughirah ibn Shu`abi, who said: Do not forbid the ghabqa or The two fools\n(Bayhaqi 457)"
"17305","(17305) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, who said: I asked Ibn Al-Zubair about breastfeeding, and he said: Do not enter ihram. Breastfeeding, two breastfeedings, or three breastfeedings."
"17306","(17306) Ishaq bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Zaid, who said: Neither a breastfeeding nor a double breastfeeding is forbidden."
"17307","(17307) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yassar, who said: It is forbidden from it what is separated. Intestines"
"17308","(17308) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abu Amr Al-Shaybani, he said: Abdullah said: He only makes ihram from Breastfeeding does not make the flesh grow and the bones grow."
"17309","(17309) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: Abu Musa said: Breastfeeding is not forbidden except as long as the flesh has grown. And blood."
"17310","(17310) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: When Aisha wanted someone to enter upon her, She ordered him to be breastfed, so she ordered Umm Kulthum to breastfeed Salim ten times, so she breastfed him three times, and she fell ill, but he did not enter. She ordered Fatima bint Umar to breastfeed Asim ibn Saad, their servant, ten times, so she breastfed him and he entered. Aliyah (Abdul Razzaq 13929)"
"17311","(17311) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of his followers, who said: I wrote to Abraham asking him about breastfeeding, so he wrote Until Ali and Abdullah used to say: A little and a lot of it is forbidden."
"17312","(17312) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid. Ibn Masoud said: It is forbidden to breastfeed a little, just as it is forbidden to breastfeed a little. Many, and Mujahid said: The saying of Ibn Masoud is more beloved to me."
"17313","(17313) Waki’ told us on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abbas, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas being asked about a woman breastfeeding a boy. Breastfeeding, and he said: If the boy is unmarried, she will be forbidden to him, and she will not give birth to him."
"17314","(17314) Ishaq bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hanzali, on the authority of Tawus, who said: He stipulated ten breastfeedings, then it was said: The two breastfeedings One is forbidden."
"17315","(17315) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’ba, who said: Al-Hakam and Hammad said: Mastah is forbidden."
"17316","(17316) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: I asked Ibn Abbas, and he said: One woman. You forbid"
"17317","(17317) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, he said: I asked Ibn Umar, and he said: A single mastic makes you forbidden."
"17318","(17318) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’a, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of ??"
"17319","(17319) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir bin Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. I wanted to see his son Hamza bin Abdul Muttalib, and he said: She is my brother’s son through breastfeeding. He is deprived of breastfeeding as much as he is deprived of lineage. (Bukhari 2445. Muslim 13)"
"17320","(17320) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ali, who said: I said: O Messenger of God, why do you bother with Quraysh and leave us? He said: Do you have something? I said: Yes, his son Hamza, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: She is not permissible for me, for she is the daughter of my brother through breastfeeding. (Muslim 11. Ahmad 1/82)"
"17321","(17321) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha, who said: My uncle came to me from breastfeeding. Aflah bin Abi Al-Qu'ais asked permission to come to me after the veil was drawn, but I refused to give him permission until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon me. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: He is your uncle, so he gave him permission. She said: The woman breastfed me and the man did not breastfeed me. He said: I was raised. Your hand, or your right hand. (Muslim 1069. Ibn Majah 1948)"
"17322","(17322) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Zainab bint Umm Salama, on the authority of Umm Salama that Umm Habibah said: O Messenger of God, do you have anything to do with my sister, your son Abu Sufyan? He said: She is not permissible for me. She said: I have been informed that you are proposing marriage to Durra, the daughter of Abi Salma. He said: The daughter of Abi Salma? She said: Yes, he said: By God, if she is not my stepdaughter under my guardianship, she is not lawful for me. She is my foster-brother’s son. She nursed me and her father is my daughter, so do not present to me your daughters or your sisters.\n(Bukhari 5106 and Muslim 1072)"
"17323","(17323) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: Aisha used to prohibit breastfeeding as many times as she prohibited from breastfeeding. Childbirth"
"17324","(17324) Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ayyub, he said: My uncle Iyas bin Amir narrated to me, he said: Ali said: Do not marry Whoever has been breastfed by your brother’s wife, nor by your father’s wife, nor by your son’s wife."
"17325","(17325) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Abdul Al-Ala, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas He said: He is forbidden from breastfeeding what is forbidden from lineage."
"17326","(17326) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He is forbidden from breastfeeding what is forbidden from breastfeeding. lineage"
"17327","(17327) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abdullah bin Utbah, who said: I see it, on the authority of Abdul God said: He is forbidden from breastfeeding what is forbidden from lineage."
"17328","(17328) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Irrak ibn Malik, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What is forbidden through breastfeeding is forbidden through lineage. (Muslim 9. Ibn Majah 1937)"
"17329","(17329) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdul-Ala, who said: I heard Suwayd bin Ghafali. He says: He is forbidden from breastfeeding what is forbidden from lineage."
"17330","(17330) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’ that it was said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Do you have anything to do with the daughter of Hamza? He said: She is not permissible for me. She is my brother’s son through breastfeeding. (Bukhari 4251)"
"17331","(۱۷۳۳۱) حَدَّثَنَا حَفْصٌ ، عَنِ الشَّیْبَانِیِّ ، عَنْ أَبِی الضُّحَی ، عَنْ أَبِی عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ ، عَنِ ابْنِ مَسْعُودٍ قَالَ : لاَ"
"17332","(۱۷۳۳۲) حَدَّثَنَا أَبُو الأَحْوَصِِ ، عَنْ مُغِیرَۃَ ، عَنْ إبْرَاہِیمَ قَالَ قَالَ عَبْدُ اللہِ لاَ رَضَاعَ إلاَّ مَا کَانَ فِی The two years."
"17333","(17333) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Zubaid, he said: Ali said: It is not forbidden from breastfeeding except what is in it. The two years."
"17334","(17334) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: There is no breastfeeding except as long as it occurs within two years."
"17335","(17335) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: There is no breastfeeding after separation."
"17336","(17336) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Umar, who said: There is no breastfeeding except as long as it is childhood."
"17337","(17337) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Omar said: There is no breastfeeding after separation."
"17338","(17338) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Janab, on the authority of Ismail ibn Raja`, on the authority of al-Nazzal ibn Sabra, on the authority of Ali, who said: No. Breastfeeding after separation."
"17339","(17339) Abdou told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdul Rahman bin Hatib, on the authority of his grandfather that He asked Umm Salama about breastfeeding, and she said: No breastfeeding except as long as it was in the cradle before weaning."
"17340","(17340) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, that Abu Hurairah was asked about breastfeeding, and he said: He does not deprive someone of Breastfeeding, except for what has broken the intestines and was in the breast before weaning."
"17341","(17341) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hajjaj ibn Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. In the same way"
"17342","(17342) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Urwah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Hajjaj, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, similarly"
"17343","(17343) Ibn Mahdi and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, that Alqamiya passed With a woman who is breastfeeding a boy of hers after two years, and he said: Do not give her any disease to drink."
"17344","(17344) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If a boy is weaned, then there is no breastfeeding after weaning."
"17345","(17345) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah Ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: He is not forbidden from breastfeeding except that which is In childhood"
"17346","(17346) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: There is no breastfeeding except what is in The cradle, otherwise it would not produce flesh and blood."
"17347","(17347) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Whatever breastfeeding or snus during the two years is considered breastfeeding, Whatever happened after that is not breastfeeding."
"17348","(17348) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdullah and Hasan, the sons of Muhammad, on the authority of their father, that Ali said To Ibn Abbas: Did you not know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the meat of domestic donkeys?\n(Bukhari 4216. Muslim 29)"
"17349","(17349) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Sabra Al-Jinni, on the authority of his father, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the intercourse with women on the Day of Conquest. (Muslim 26. Abu Dawud 2066)"
"17350","(17350) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar, on the authority of al-Rabi’ ibn Sabrā, on the authority of his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was standing between the corner and the door and saying: O people, I have given you permission to do so. Enjoyment, for God has forbidden them until the Day of Resurrection, so whoever has any of them let him leave his way and do not Take something from what you have been given.\n(Muslim 25. Ibn Majah 1962)"
"17351","(17351) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad, who said: Abu Al-Umays narrated to us, on the authority of Ias bin Salama, On the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, permitted three footsteps in pleasure every year, then forbade them.\n(Muslim 18 Ahmad 4/55)"
"17352","(17352) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Umar said: If I had come forward In it I was stoned, meaning the mutati."
"17353","(17353) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: Omar forbade, on the authority of Mut’a’in Mut’a an-Nisa’. And the enjoyment of Hajj."
"17354","(17354) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, who said: He was asked about women’s sexual intercourse, and he said: No. We know it except the incestuous person."
"17355","(17355) Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he was asked about mut’a, and he said: It is forbidden, and he was told: Indeed, Ibn Abbas issued a fatwa on her, so he said: So do not insist on her during the time of your life."
"17356","(17356) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab that he said: May God have mercy on Omar, had he not He forbade, fornication became open."
"17357","(17357) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: By God, the period of enjoyment lasted only three days. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave them permission to do so, whether before or after that. (Abdul Razzaq 14040)"
"17358","(17358) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Al-Walid narrated to me, saying: Ibn Dhu’ayb said to me: I heard Ibn Al-Zubair delivers a sermon and says: The wolf’s nickname is Abu Ja’adah, but mut’a is fornication."
"17359","(17359) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Omar, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muslim, on the authority of Tawus, who said: It was the Sunnah of Mut’a is the law of marriage, except that the term is in our hands."
"17360","(17360) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of his father, who said: Omar said: If you brought a man who would enjoy With a woman, I would stone him if he was chaste, but if he was not chaste, I would strike him."
"17361","(17361) Shababah ibn Siwar narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn al-Ghaz, who said: I heard an alcoholic saying about a man who gets married. The woman for a certain period of time. He said: That is adultery."
"17362","(17362) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Qais, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted us while we were young. We said: O Messenger of God, shall we not seek emasculation? He said: No. Then he granted us permission to marry a woman with the garment for a specified period. Then Abdullah recited: {O you who have believed, do not deprive Good things that God has made lawful for you."
"17363","(17363) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Musayyab ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Qubaisa ibn Jabir, on the authority of Omar, he said: No. He was given a halal, and there was no halal for him except you stoned them both."
"17364","(17364) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha’, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn Umar that he said: May God curse him. What is permissible, what is permissible for it, and what is permissible for it."
"17365","(17365) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Aroub, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abd Al-Malik ibn al-Mughirah ibn Nawfal said that Ibn Umar was asked about a woman’s permissibility for her husband, and he said: That incestuous person, if Omar has come to you so that we may talk to you."
"17366","(17366) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Shihab, on the authority of Jabala ibn Da`laj, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, who said: The analyst is cursed."
"17367","(17367) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim and Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan. They said: If one of the three is tempted, he becomes corrupt. Sexual intercourse"
"17368","(17368) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a man who married a woman to make her lawful. To her husband, so the arbitrator said: Let him hold her, and Hammad said: I would love for him to separate from her."
"17369","(17369) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zaid, about a man who married a woman in order to make her permissible. To her husband, and he did not know, he said: This is not valid if he married her to make her permissible."
"17370","(17370) Aidh bin Habib narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: The one who makes it lawful and the one who is made lawful are cursed."
"17371","(17371) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Qays, on the authority of Huzayl, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Cursed. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the place and the permissible for him. (Tirmidhi 1820, Ahmad 1/462)"
"17372","(17372) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was cursed. May God bless him and grant him peace. (Abu Dawud 2070, Ahmad 1/83)"
"17373","(17373) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Al-Furat, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, that he was asked about a man who divorced A man from the village came to her wife, without her or her knowledge, and took out some of his money and married her to her. To make it permissible for him, and he said: No, then he mentioned that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about something like that, and he said: Not even He marries her out of desire for himself, until he marries her out of desire for himself, but if he does that, she is not lawful for him even He tastes honey."
"17374","(17374) Muadh narrated to us, saying: Abbad bin Mansour narrated to us, saying: A man came to Al-Hasan and said: A man from my people has divorced his wife. Thirdly, he regretted it and she regretted it, so I wanted to go away and marry her and be sincere with her, then enter into her as a man enters. with his wife, then divorce her until she is lawful for her husband, he said, and Al-Hasan said to him: Fear God, my boy, and do not be a nail of fire. For the limits of God."
"17375","(17375) Al-Mu’alla bin Mansour narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Ja’far narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman bin Muhammad Al-Akhnasi, on the authority of Al-Maqbariy. On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, cursed the one who is permissible and the one who is permissible for him.\n(Tirmidhi 437. Ahmad 2/323)"
"17376","(17376) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abu Al-Sanabel, who said: She gave birth to seven Bint Al-Harith became pregnant twenty-few nights after her husband’s death, but when she came to her senses, she saw the shame of that. And her matter was mentioned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: If she does, her time has passed.\n(Tabarani 8961 Darmi 2281)"
"17377","(17377) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Salama, who said: It was me, Ibn Abbas, and Abu Hurairah, and we remembered: A man dies, for a woman, and she gives birth shortly after his death. So I said: If she gives birth, then she is permissible. Ibn Abbas said: Her term is the last of the two terms, so they retreated accordingly. Abu Hurairah said: I am with Ibn My brother, meaning Abu Salama. So they sent Kurayb, the servant of Ibn Abbas, to Umm Salama, and she said: Your Islamic slaves have been lost. Forty nights after her husband died, and a man from Banu Abd al-Dar, nicknamed Abu al-Sanabel, proposed to her. He told her that she had become lawful and wanted to marry someone else, so Abu Al-Sanabel said to her: You have not become lawful, so she mentioned that. She was sent to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ordered her to get married. (Muslim 122. Tirmidhi 1123)"
"17378","(17378) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Miswar that Saba’i gave birth after the death of her husband In a month, she came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered her to get married. (Bukhari 5320, Ahmad 4/327)"
"17379","(17379) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, who said: He said: I heard a man from the Ansar speaking to Ibn Umar. He says: I heard your father saying: If the deceased gives birth to her husband with her stomach while he is on the bed, then it is permissible."
"17380","(17380) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mawīb, on the authority of Salih ibn Kaysan, on the authority of Omar And Othman said: If it is placed on the side of the house in its shrouds, then it is permissible."
"17381","(17381) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab that Umar consulted Ali ibn Abu Talib, may God be pleased with him, and Zaid bin Thabit. Zaid said: It is permissible, and Ali said: Four months and ten days. Zaid said: Have you seen? If she was dead, Ali said: At the last of the two terms, Omar said: If she had placed her womb and her husband on his bier, he would not have entered. If you dug it, it would have been solved."
"17382","(17382) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, he said: Abdullah said: By God, whoever wishes, I will share it with him. Surat An-Nisa’ Al-Qasra was revealed after four months and ten days. (Abu Dawud 2301 and Ibn Majah 2030)"
"17383","(17383) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, that he said regarding her husband who died, and Pregnant: If she gives birth, she is permissible."
"17384","(17384) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say: If a man divorces his wife while she is pregnant, Or he died on her behalf, then her term is for her to give birth."
"17385","(17385) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Abdullah said: It is permissible for every pregnant woman to give birth. He said: And Ali used to say: The last of the two terms."
"17386","(17386) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, and no stolen property was mentioned in it, on the authority of Ali that it was He says: The last of the two terms."
"17387","(17387) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Amr ibn Salem, who said: Ubayy ibn Ka’b said: O Messenger of God, there are a number of Of the number of women not mentioned in the Book of God, the young, the old, and pregnant women, then God Almighty revealed: {And those who despair of The menstruating woman among your women, if you are in doubt, then her period is three months. And those who have not menstruated and those who are pregnant have a term for them to give birth. They carried us}"
"17388","(17388) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: I was in a meeting where Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi was present. For Layla, he said: He said: The last of the two terms. He said: So I mentioned the hadith of Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Saba’. He said, so his companions gathered together for him. He said: So I said: I would be bold against Abdullah bin Utbah if I lied to him while he was near the mosque.\n(Bukhari 4532. An-Nasa’i 5715)"
"17389","(17389) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, regarding a pregnant woman whose husband has died: Her waiting period is the last of the two terms."
"17390","(17390) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of his father, who said: She gave birth to his seven lions after his death. He married her off for twenty, or for a month, or something like that. Then Abu Al-Sanabel ibn Baakak passed by her and said: You have been made for husbands. ? No, until four months and ten days have passed, and she came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and mentioned that to him. He said: It is permissible for wives.\n(Bukhari 5319, Bayhaqi 419)"
"17391","(17391) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Masruq and Amr bin Utba that they wrote to Suba’a bint Al-Harith. They asked her about her situation, and she wrote to them that she had given birth five years after her husband’s death. And for twenty nights, she prepared to seek goodness, so Abu Al-Sanabel ibn Baakak passed by her and said: You have hastened, another one hastened. The two terms are four months and ten. So I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, ask forgiveness for me, and he said: And what is that? So I told him the news, and he said: If you find a good husband, then marry him. (Bukhari 5319 and Muslim 1122)"
"17392","(17392) Shababah told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ubaid ibn al-Hasan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Maqil, who said: I bore witness to Ali. A man asked him about a woman whose husband died while she was pregnant. He said: She is waiting for the furthest time. A man said: The son of Masoud: Does he say that she should make herself a prisoner? Ali said: Farroukh does not know."
"17393","(17393) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah He was asked about a man who married a woman and she died, but he did not have intercourse with her and did not impose a dowry on her. Abdullah said: No. The dowry, she has the inheritance, and she has the waiting period. Ma’qil bin Yasar said: I witnessed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, judge the matter. Barwa bint Washiq is like that. (Ibn Majah 1891. Ahmad 4/280)"
"17394","(17394) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, on the authority of Abdullah: Like him\n(Abu Dawud 2108 and Ibn Majah 1891)"
"17395","(17395) Zayd bin Harun told us: Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, on the authority of Abdullah, according to something similar to the hadith of Ibn Mahdi, on the authority of Firas. (Tirmidhi 1145. Abu Dawud 2108)"
"17396","(17396) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, that Ibn Umar married his son to a woman from his family, and he died. Before he consummated the marriage with her, he did not name a friend for her, so they asked Ibn Umar for a friend, and he said: She has no friend, so they refused. They were satisfied with that, so they brought Zayd bin Thabit among them. He went to him and said: She has no dowry."
"17397","(17397) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Zayd ibn Thabit said: You inherit and observe the waiting period."
"17398","(17398) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’atha’, and Ata’ regarding the one who is entrusted to him, and he dies before To assume that they said: She has the inheritance but she has no dowry."
"17399","(17399) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr and Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abd Khayr, who is believed to have narrated it on the authority of Ali, who said: No. Inheritance and no dowry for her."
"17400","(17400) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that a man in Medina married a woman, but he did not fulfill his obligation. He did not enter into it with her. They said: She has the inheritance, but she has no dowry. Masruq said: There is no inheritance until it comes before him. Maher"
"17401","(17401) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: She is entitled to half the sadaq, or a sadaq. Abu Bakr doubted."
"17402","(17402) Ibn Abi Zaydi narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Alqamiya, who said: A man came to Ibn Masoud and said: A man among us married a woman but did not fulfill the obligation for her and did not have intercourse with her until he died. Ibn Masoud said: I was not asked about anything. Since I left the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, something has been more difficult for me than this. Ask someone else, and they hesitated there for a month. He said: Then he said: Who? I ask, are you, my brothers, companions of Muhammad in this country? He said: I will speak about it according to my opinion. If it is correct, then it is from God, and if it is wrong, then it is from me and from Satan. I think that it has The dowry of her wives, neither of them nor any deductions, and she is entitled to the inheritance, and she is required to count the number of her husband who died. He said: Some of the most courageous people: We bear witness that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made a judgment like the one you made regarding a woman from among us who was called “the splendor of his son.” Washiq said: I never saw Ibn Masoud happy with anything, as he was not happy with it at that time. (Ibn Hibban 4101, Hakim 180)"
"17403","(17403) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: A son of Abdullah bin Umar married a daughter of Ubaid Allah. Ibn Omar, whose mother was Asmaa bint Zayd Ibn Al-Khattab, so she died, and he had not imposed on her a dowry, so they asked him for a dowry. And the inheritance. Ibn Umar said: She has the inheritance but no dowry for her. So they refused that to Ibn Umar, so they put Zayd bin among them. Thabit, so Zaid said: She has the inheritance and no dowry for her."
"17404","(17404) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abd Khayr, on the authority of Ali, who said: She has the inheritance and no dowry. No"
"17405","(17405) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In the case of a woman whose husband dies before he fulfills the obligation for her and before he consummates the marriage with her: that she has the right to dowry with her wives. And he narrates that, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who promised the deceased and she has the inheritance. (Saeed bin Mansour 933 and Abdul Razzaq 10900)"
"17406","(17406) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of the one who informed him, on the authority of Ali, who said: For her Inheritance and no dowry for her."
"17407","Abu Abdul Rahman Buqi bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Abu Bakr Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abi Shaybah told us, he said:\n(17407) Ja’far bin Aoun told us, saying: Rabi’i bin Uthman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of Nahar Al-Abdi, who was one of the companions of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, on the authority of Abu Sa’id that a man brought his son to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: This daughter of mine refused to get married. He said: So he said to her: Obey your father. He said: She said: Not even. Can you tell me what rights a husband has over his wife? She repeated what she said to him, and he said: The husband’s right over his wife is that if he had an ulcer, she licked it, or he licked it. There was pus or blood in his nostrils. Then she licked him as she had fulfilled her duty. He said, and she said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I will never marry. He said, and he said. Do not marry them except with their permission. (Ibn Hibban 4164 Hakim 188)"
"17408","(17408) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Abu Nasr Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Masawar al-Himyari, on the authority of his mother, who said : I heard Umm Salamah saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Whatever woman dies and her husband is satisfied with her. You entered Paradise. (Tirmidhi 1161. Tabarani 884)"
"17409","(17409) Abd al-Rahman bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: She came The wife of the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Messenger of God, what is the husband’s right over his wife? He said: She does not prevent herself from doing so, even if she were on the back of a cloth. She said: O Messenger of God, what is the husband’s right over his wife? He said: Do not give in charity anything from his household except with His permission. If she does so, he will have the reward and the burden will be upon her. She said: O Prophet of God, what The right of the husband over his wife. He said: She shall not leave his house except with his permission. If she does so, the angels of God and the angels of mercy will curse her. And your angels are angry until you repent, or withdraw. She said: O Prophet of God, what if he was unjust to her? He said: Even if he was unjust to her, she said: By the One who sent you with the truth, no one will have control over my affairs after this, as long as I remain with him."
"17410","(17410) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Bashir bin Yassar, on the authority of Husayn bin Muhsin Her paternal aunt came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, seeking a need. When she had fulfilled her need, he said: Do you have a husband? She said: Yes, he said: Where are you from it? She said: I have not given him anything good except what I am unable to do. He said: Look, for it is your Paradise and your Hell.\n(Ahmad 4/341, Hakim 189)"
"17411","(17411) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, who said: When Muadh came from Yemen, he said: O Messenger of God We saw people prostrating to one another, so shall we not prostrate to you? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No, no one should prostrate to anyone besides God, and if I were to command someone to prostrate to anyone, I would command. Women prostrate to their husbands."
"17412","(17412) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of a man from the Ansar, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, similar to the hadith of Abu Muawiyah. (Ibn Majah 1853; Harith 498)"
"17413","(17413) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, who said: Do not exceed three. The prayer of one of them is his head, an imam or the mother of a group of people who are reluctant to him, a woman who disobeys her husband, and a slave escaping from his master."
"17414","(17414) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Qur’a ibn Khalid, on the authority of a woman from Banu Attarid called Rabi’i’, who said: She said: Aisha: O people of women, if you knew the rights of your husbands over you, you would make the women among you wipe the dust from your face. He married her freely."
"17415","(17415) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, on the authority of Ziyad bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith bin Al-Mustaliq said: It used to be said: The most severely tormented people are two: a woman who disobeys her husband and the imam of a people and their family. A hater"
"17416","(17416) Ali bin Mushir told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of his mother, who said: The women of the people of Medina were They built a woman over her husband, starting with Aisha, so we brought her in to her, and she would place her hand on her head and pray for her. And you command her to fear God and fulfill the rights of her husband."
"17417","(17417) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul Malik, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: It is not appropriate for anything to prostrate to anything, and if that were the case, the women would be for their husbands."
"17418","(17418) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: If a man invites his wife to his bed and she refuses and spends the night angry with her, the angels curse her until Good morning\n(Bukhari 5193, Muslim 122)"
"17419","(17419) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ali bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Aisha said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command the woman to She should prostrate to her husband, even if a man ordered his wife to move from a red mountain to a black mountain, or from a black mountain to another. A red mountain. We had given her that she would do it."
"17420","(17420) Mulazim bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Badr, on the authority of Qais bin Talq, on the authority of his father Talq bin Ali, who said: We sat with the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I heard the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: If a man calls his wife For his need, let it come to him, even if it is on the stove. (Tirmidhi 1160. Ahmad 4/23)"
"17421","(17421) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to say: If only a woman had sucked the nose of Her husband is suffering from leprosy until she dies, as long as she fulfills her rights."
"17422","(17422) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, who said: I heard al-Qasim bin Mukhammara mention Some people brought Salman to him so that he might lead them in prayer, but he refused until they pushed him away. When he led them in prayer, he said: Are all of you satisfied? They said: Yes. He said: Praise be to God. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: There are three whose prayers will not be accepted: A woman leaves her husband’s house without his permission, and a fugitive slave, or a man, leads a group of people and they have haters."
"17423","(17423) Ali bin Hassan bin Shaqiq narrated to us, saying: Husayn bin Waqid narrated to me, saying: Abu Ghalib narrated to us, on the authority of Abi Imam, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There are three whose prayers will not exceed their ears until they return: the absent servant. And a woman spent the night while her husband was angry with her and the imam of a people, and they hated him."
"17424","(17424) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Zaid bin Wahhab, who said: Omar wrote to us: A woman should not fast. Voluntarily, except with her permission, meaning her husband."
"17425","(17425) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Do not fast voluntarily while he is present. Except with her permission, meaning her husband."
"17426","(17426) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Yahya bin Ja’di, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: It is good. The benefit a Muslim will benefit from after becoming a Muslim is a beautiful woman who pleases him when he looks at her, obeys him when he commands her, and protects him. If he is absent from her in his wealth and life. (Abu Dawud 1661, Saeed bin Mansour 501)"
"17427","(17427) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Muawiyah ibn Qurayh, on the authority of his father, he said: Omar said: No man has benefited. Or a servant said, “After believing in God, he is better than a woman of good character, affectionate, and affectionate.” And no man benefits after disbelief in God. worse than a woman of bad character and sharp tongue. Then he said: Among them are sheep from which he does not shoo, and among them is a sheep that he will ransom. From him"
"17428","(17428) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, who said: Like a mirror. A good woman to a righteous man is like a crown set with gold on the head of a king, and a bad mirror to a righteous man is like a lamb. It is difficult for the great sheikh."
"17429","(17429) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Abu Moses said: There are three whom they call upon, but they will not be answered: A man who gave his wealth to a fool, and God, Blessed and Most High, said: {And do not give Fools, your wealth} and a man who had a woman of bad character but did not divorce her, or did not separate from her, and a man who was He has a right over a man, but he did not bear witness against him."
"17430","(17430) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abu Nasr Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Amr said: Shall I not inform you of the three Faqiqir? He said: What are they? He said: An unjust imam. If you do good, he does not thank you, and if you do wrong, he does not forgive him. He is an unjust imam. If he sees a good deed, he covers it, even if he sees it. A bad woman, if you see her, she will anger you, and if you are absent from her, she will betray you."
"17431","(17431) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ja’dah ibn Hubayra that whenever he married any of his daughters alone He forbade her from bad behavior and commanded her to do better."
"17432","(17432) Zaid bin Harun told us: Shayban told us, Abd al-Malik bin Umair told us, on the authority of Zaid bin Uqba, on the authority of Samra bin Jundub, who said: I heard Omar bin Al-Khattab say: There are three types of women: a soft, soft woman. She is chaste, Muslim, friendly, and affectionate. She helps her family forever, but does not help her family forever, and you rarely find her. Secondly: A chaste Muslim woman who only has a vessel for the child and has nothing else. Thirdly: A lice cap. God places it on the neck of whomever He wishes, and no one else will take it away. The men are three: a chaste, Muslim, sane man who commands Regarding matters, if they occur and become similar, then when they occur, he comes out of them with his own opinion, and a chaste Muslim man has no opinion. The matter came to him with his opinion and advice, so he consulted him and consulted him, then he came down to his command, and he was a confused and wandering man who did not seek guidance or guidance. He obeys a guide."
"17433","(17433) Abdul Malik bin Abi Suleiman told us, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: A woman may be married for her religion, her wealth, and her beauty, so you must do so for the same religion. Your hands are dusty. (Muslim 1087, Tirmidhi 1086)"
"17434","(17434) Khaled bin Mukhlid told us, saying: Muhammad bin Musa Al-Madani told me, saying: Saad bin Ishaq told me, about His paternal aunt, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A woman may be married on one of three characteristics: A woman may be married for her wealth, for her beauty, she may be married for her religion, for the same religion and character that your right hand is blessed with.\n(Hakim 1611, Ahmad 3/80)"
"17435","(17435) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Yahya bin Ja’diyah, who said: A woman may be married to Her religion, her morals, her wealth, her beauty, how can I be with you, with the same morals and religion, your right hand is dusted. (Saeed bin Mansour 502)"
"17436","(17436) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Yahya bin Ja’diyah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: A woman may be married for her wealth, for her lineage, for her beauty, and for her religion, so you must be brought up in the same religion. Your right"
"17437","(17437) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: If one of you, when he wanted to go to your family, said: In the name of God, O God, spare us Satan and protect us. We have not provided for Satan, for if a child were born between them, Satan would never harm him. (Bukhari 3271, Muslim 116)"
"17438","(17438) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa`id, the servant of Abu Asid, who said: I got married I was a slave, so I called a group of the Prophet’s companions, may God bless him and grant him peace. Among them were Ibn Masoud, Abu Dharr and Hudhayf. He said: And the prayer was performed. He said: So Abu Dharr went to come forward, and they said: To you. He said: Or like that? They said: Yes, he said: So I approached them while I was a slave slave, and they taught me, and they said: When your family comes to you, pray for you. Pray two rak'ahs, then ask God Almighty for the good that has befallen you, and seek refuge in Him from the evil of it. Then, take care of yourself and your family."
"17439","(17439) Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of my nephew Alqamiya bin Qais, on the authority of You taught me that when Ibn Masoud cheated on his family, he would descend and say: Oh God, do not give Satan a share in what You have provided for us."
"17440","(17440) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Umm Salamah, who said: She used not to marry in Medina as a maid to her husband. Until he passes her in the mosque and you pray in it. Abu Bakr said: He said: I see him saying: Two rak’ahs, and until he passes by her on The wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they pray for her."
"17441","(17441) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, who said: A man called Abu Jarir came to Abdullah. He said: I married my maid when I was young, and I fear that she will leave me alone. He said: Abdullah said: The love is from God and the love is from God. Satan wants to force to you what God has made lawful for you, so when she comes to you, tell her, then pray two rak’ahs behind you."
"17442","(17442) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Mujahid, in his saying: {And do not hold back. With the protection of the infidels.} He said: If a Muslim’s wife joins the polytheists, none of his wives will be taken care of by her."
"17443","(17443) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, similar to him."
"17444","(17444) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Abd al-Rahman bin Awf: Did he know even a sheep, that is, when he got married? (Bukhari 2049, Abu Dawud 2102)"
"17445","(17445) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of a statement, he said: I heard Anas say: The children of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, so he sent me and I invited men to eat. (Bukhari 5170, Tirmidhi 3219)"
"17446","(17446) Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: When Bilal married, he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. With gold, he said to Bilal: Give this a drink, then he said: Help your brother in his feast. (Abu Dawud 2268, Saeed bin Mansour 588)"
"17447","(17447) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansur bin Safiyya, on the authority of his mother, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He married some of his wives with a sack of barley. (Nasa’i 6607. Ahmad 6/113)"
"17448","(17448) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hafsa, who said: When my father got married, Sirin called the companions of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him for seven days, and when the Day of the Ansar came, he called them and called Ubayy ibn Ka’b and Zayd ibn Thabit. He said Hisham: And I think he said, and Muadh said: Ubayy was fasting, so when they had eaten, he called Ubayy ibn Ka’b and made the people safe."
"17449","(17449) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was in pain. He greeted Zainab and satisfied the Muslims with bread and meat. (Bukhari 4793 and Muslim 1048)"
"17450","(17450) Affan narrated to us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman narrated to us, he said: Malik bin Dinar narrated to me, he said: An old man from the neighborhood narrated to me. She said: Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari married some of his sons. She said: So he made a vow over it and invited people."
"17451","(17451) Jarir told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Ibn Umar used to encourage the circumcision of boys."
"17452","(17452) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Isra’il, on the authority of Al-A’mash, that Abu Wa’il: He was the head of a cow and four people. Loaves"
"17453","(17453) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem ibn Abdullah, who said: I was married. During the time of my father, my father called the people to prayer, and he was among those who gave the call to prayer to Abu Ayyub."
"17454","(17454) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Yunus Al-Alayli, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim that Hamza bin Abdullah bin Omar made a massive sacrifice."
"17455","(17455) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Omar bin Hamza, he said: Salem bin Abdullah told me, he said: My father circumcised me. And Nu'aym bin Abdullah slaughtered a ram for us, and you saw us arguing with him over the young men."
"17456","(17456) It was narrated to us that Abdou bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: It was said: His servant Daughter of Hakim, one of those who dedicated themselves to the Prophet, peace be upon him. (Bukhari 5113. Muslim 50)"
"17457","(17457) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid: {And a believing woman, if she gives her soul To the Prophet} He said: She did not fear herself."
"17458","(17458) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam. He said: Abd al-Malik wrote to the people of Medina, asking them. He said: Then Ali wrote to him. Shu’ba said: And you thought he was the son of Hussein. He said: Aban bin Taghlib told me, on the authority of The ruling is that Ali bin Hussein said: She is a woman from Azd, who is called the mother of a partner, and she gave herself to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace.\n(Nasa’i 8928 and Ahmad 6/462)"
"17459","(17459) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said: Abdullah bin Abi Al-Safar narrated to me, on the authority of Shu’abi, that she is a woman from The Ansar gave themselves to the Prophet, and they were among those who deferred."
"17460","(17460) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of his people, he said: And the people of Medina narrated to me that they used to say to the thing: Lao. Greater in life than that of Umm Sharik."
"17461","(17461) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b, Omar bin Al-Hakam, and Abdullah bin His servants said: The one who gave herself to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, is Maymun. (Tabari 23. Bayhaqi 55)"
"17462","(17462) Shababah ibn Siwar narrated to us, on the authority of Warqa’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid: {And a believing woman, if And she gave herself to the Prophet} He said: without giving alms."
"17463","(17463) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid: (And a believing woman, if she gives her soul to the Prophet) He said: She did it and he did not do it."
"17464","(17464) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Awf, who said: Two Umarish sheikhs from the circles of Qusama bin Zuhayr narrated to us that Hammam Ibn Umair is a man from the Banu Taym Allah who united two sisters in the pre-Islamic era and did not separate one of them. Until there was a disagreement with Omar, and he raised his status to Omar, so he sent to him and said: Choose one of them, by God, if it is near. The last time I will hit your head."
"17465","(17465) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If he converts to Islam and has two sisters, he can imprison the first of them if he wishes."
"17466","(17466) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Farwa, on the authority of Abu Wahb al-Jishani, on the authority of Abu Kharash Al-Ra'aniyi, on the authority of Al-Dailami, who said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I have two sisters whom I married in The pre-Islamic one, and he said: If she comes back, divorce one of them. (Tirmidhi 1129. Ahmad 4/232)"
"17467","(17467) Ibn Aliyah and Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Az-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Ghaylan bin Salamah Al-Thaqafi and ten women under him converted to Islam, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Take four from them.\n(Dar Qatni 271, Bayhaqi 183)"
"17468","(17468) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who embraces Islam when he has ten or six women, he said: He may keep four of them."
"17469","(17469) Bakr bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, saying: Issa bin Al-Mukhtar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Humaidha Ibn Al-Shamardal, on the authority of Qais Ibn Al-Harith Al-Asadi, that he converted to Islam and had eight wives, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded him to do so. He granted permission to choose four from among them. (Abu Dawud 2236. Ibn Majah 1952)"
"17470","(17470) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, in his saying: {other than those who have the right to usury}. He said: the one who has not reached I want him to look at the private parts of women."
"17471","(17471) Ibn Idris narrated to us, I think, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said in his statement: {other than those in charge of usury}. He said:"
"17472","(17472) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, in his saying: “Other than those who are entitled to usury from Men} He said: He who has no interest in women."
"17473","(17473) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, who said: The idiot"
"17474","(17474) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He is the one they say: He is a fool."
"17475","(17475) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: He is the one who does not Women feel ashamed of him."
"17476","(17476) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Aoun, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: He is the one against whom no one can stand."
"17477","(17477) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: Omar bin Al-Khattab separated them and made friends between them. The House of Money, and Al-Zuhri said: Her friendship was not in the House of Money, it is because of what happened to her private parts."
"17478","(17478) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Salih bin Muslim, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, he said: Omar said: He will separate them and make They made friends with her in the treasury, and Ali said: There will be a separation between them, and she has the friendship for what she has made lawful of her private parts."
"17479","(17479) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: He will separate them and her. Friendship with what is permissible from her private parts."
"17480","(17480) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar, who said: He should separate them. Zakat is thrown into the treasury."
"17481","(17481) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Every marriage is corrupt, like... The one who marries her and her relatives during her waiting period, this is an invalid marriage. If he has consummated the marriage with her, then she gets the dowry and it will be separated. Between them."
"17482","(17482) Yahya bin Abdul-Malik bin Abi Ghaniyā told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hakam that he said: It separates Between her and her husband, and she will have the dowry based on what she has made lawful from her private parts."
"17483","(17483) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, who said: A lifespan was passed regarding a woman who got married in He promised her that he would separate them as long as they lived and that he would put their friendship in the treasury, and he said: Her marriage was forbidden, so they made friends with her. It was forbidden, and Ali decided that they should be separated and he died, counting what was left of the first husband, then she should wait for three qurā’s. She has the right to dowry for what he has permitted of her private parts, and then if he wishes, he can propose to her after that."
"17484","(۱۷۴۸۴) حَدَّثَنَا وَکِیعٌ ، عَنْ سُفْیَانَ ، عَنْ أَبِی حَصِینٍ ، عَنْ عَبْدِ اللہِ بْنِ حَبِیبٍ قَالَ : خَرَجَ رَسُولُ اللہِ صَلَّی اللَّہُ عَلَیْہِ وَسَلَّمَ فَلَقِیَ امْرَأَۃً فَأَعْجَبَتْہُ فَرَجَعَ إلَی أُمِّ سَلَمَۃَ وَعِنْدَہَا نِسْوَۃٌ یَدُفن طِیبًا قَالَ : فَعَرَفْنَ فِی وَجْہِہِ فَأَخْلَیْنَہُ فَقَضَی حَاجَتَہُ فَخَرَجَ ، فَقَالَ : مَنْ رَأَی مِنْکُمُ امْرَأَۃً فَأَعْجَبَتْہُ فَلِیَأْتِ"
"17485","(17485) Abdul Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Abdullah bin Habib, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, similar to the hadith of Abu Husayn, except that he did not mention: He should be buried well."
"17486","(17486) Waki’ and Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hallam, who said: “Abd said: God: Whoever among you sees a woman and she likes her, he will have intercourse with her family, for they are like those who are with them. (Dharmi 2215)"
"17487","(17487) Ubaidah narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Jaad that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw A woman, so he came to Umm Salama, so he touched her and said: If one of you sees a woman who admires her, let her go to her family, for they are like The one who is with them."
"17488","(17488) Abdul Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, similar to the hadith of Abdullah.\n(Muslim 9. Abu Dawud 2144)"
"17489","(17489) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Mutarrif about a man who sees a woman who admires him. He said: He mentions the calves of cows."
"17490","(17490) Zaid bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Ibrahim, regarding the man who sees The woman was amazed. He said: It is a mention of our blessings."
"17491","(17491) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Ali bin Mudrak, who said: I heard Al-Nakha’i say: Al-Ash’ath married a woman. On its ruling, it was brought to Omar bin Al-Khattab, and he said: Her land is her land."
"17492","(17492) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If a man marries a woman according to her rulings, Or the ruling of an unrighteous person in friendship, or they are unjust, return that person to a friend like her, neither indecent nor extravagant, and marriage is permissible."
"17493","(17493) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, who said: Amr ibn Harith proposed to Adi ibn Hatim his daughter, but he refused except to judge him. So Amr went back and consulted his companions, and they said: Do you want to judge a man who has intercourse with him? He made a marriage contract with you, but he refused, so he married her according to his ruling, then he left and Adi ruled according to the Sunnah of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Four hundred and eighty, so Amr sent him ten thousand and said: Prepare them."
"17494","(17494) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin that Al-Ash’ath married a woman according to her ruling, so Omar asked him About her, and he said: I spent the night that no one knows except God, fearing that you would judge me regarding the wealth of Qays, so he said: That is not the case. No, she only gets the dowry of her wives."
"17495","(17495) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, about Ata’ regarding a man who married a woman according to her ruling. So the woman died before the man could rule. He said: She has the dowry of her wives."
"17496","(17496) Ali told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’ regarding a man who married a woman according to her ruling, so he ruled ten times. Dharam said: It is permissible, as Muslims used to marry people who were less than that or more."
"17497","(17497) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sari bin Yahya, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: One man said to another: By companionship and children, Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not say like that, say: God bless you and bless you."
"17498","(17498) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that Aqeel bin Abi Talib married a woman from Banu Jashm So he summoned them and they said: With the companions and the children. So he said: Do not say that. They said: How should we say that, O Abu Yazid? He said: You say: May God bless you and bless you, for we used to say, or were commanded to do so. (Ibn Majah 1906; Ahmad 1/451)"
"17499","(17499) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus bin Ubaid, on the authority of Amr bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Zur’i bin Amr, on the authority of Jarir said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about my sudden sight, and he ordered me to avert my gaze.\n(Muslim 1499; Abu Dawud 2141)"
"17500","(17500) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Suwayd, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Ziyad, who said: It used to be said: Do not follow your good eyesight. A woman’s dress, for looking creates lust in the heart."
"17501","(17501) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: (Tell the believers to lower their gaze) I said: According to Al-Shaabi: A man looks at a mirror but does not see anything forbidden in it. He said: Why should you pierce it with your eyes?"
"17502","(17502) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The desires of the heart look at it, so there is no good in it."
"17503","(17503) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Rabi` al-Iyadi, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ali: Do not follow one look with another, for you only have the first and you do not have the last. (Tirmidhi) 2777. Abu Dawud 2142)"
"17504","(17504) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Musa Al-Janni, who said: I was with Saeed bin Jubayr on the road. Then a woman or a female servant met us. He said: We all looked at her. Then Sa`id lowered his gaze and I looked at him. He said: Then Sa`id said to him: The first is for you and the second is against you."
"17505","(17505) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: It used to be said: No one owns the first theory. But the one who deceives the gaze."
"17506","(17506) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud Abi Al-Haytham, who said: A man said to Ibn Sirin: I face the qiblah on the road, isn’t it? Why do I have the first glance and then turn my gaze away from her? He said: Have you not read the Qur’an: {They lower their gazes} {The eyes know the traitors of you, and what the breasts conceal}"
"17507","(17507) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Mahduj, who said: I heard Anas say: When you meet a woman, lower your eyes. Until you pass"
"17508","(17508) Abdul-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: The beauty of a woman will not harm you as long as you do not know her."
"17509","(17509) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Amr bin Saeed, he said: Saad bin Abi Waqqas said: While I am going around At home, I saw a woman and I liked her. I liked her, so I wanted to ask about her, but I found her busy, and Hasan will not harm you. A woman you do not know."
"17510","(17510) Ismail bin Shuaib told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Tawus that he disliked a man looking at a woman except To be a husband or a mahram."
"17511","(17511) Abu Asama told us, saying: Abu Umair told me, on the authority of Ayoub, who said: There was a peacock who did not accompany a companion. A woman"
"17512","(17512) Affan narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salma narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Salma bin Abu Tufayl, on the authority of Ali, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Ali, you have a treasure in Paradise, and you are Its two horns, so do not follow the look to the other, for you only have the first and you do not have the last. (Ahmad 1/1591 Darmi 2709)"
"17513","(17513) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, he said: Ibn Abbas said: {He knows the traitor of the eyes, and what the breasts hide} He said: The man He will be among the people, and a woman will pass by them and he will show them that he will lower his gaze from her, but if he sees any of them heedless, he will look. If he fears that they will discover him, he lowers his gaze, and God has seen from his heart that he wishes to look at her private parts."
"17514","(17514) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Amr Al-Shaybani, he said: Abu Musa said: Because my nostrils are filled with The smell of a carrion is more beloved to me than being filled with the smell of a woman."
"17515","(17515) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah said: Because I would like to push a camel covered with tar To prevent me from crowding a woman."
"17516","(17516) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Thabit bin Amara, on the authority of Ghanim bin Qais, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: Every eye Fa`aliyah means adulteress."
"17517","(17517) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In the case of a man who divorces his wife once, or twice, before he has intercourse with her, then he has an affair with her, and he believes that He returned to her. He said: Friendship is hers, and he will separate them."
"17518","(17518) Muhammad bin Sawa’i told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders; Concerning a man who divorced his wife, then he cheated on her while he believed that he had a right to take her back. He said: She has complete dowry due to his cheating. Oh her"
"17519","(17519) Muhammad bin Sawa’i told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Al-Hakam. He said: She has the full dowry."
"17520","(17520) Muhammad bin Sawa’i told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: She has the full dowry."
"17521","(17521) Muhammad bin Sawa’i told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: She has a dowry and a half."
"17522","(17522) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, regarding a man who divorced his wife before he had intercourse with her alone. Then he cheated on her while he believed that he had the right to take her back. He said: He will separate them and she will have full friendship."
"17523","(17523) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: She has a dowry and a half, and Al-Hakam said: She has Friendship"
"17524","(17524) Al-Dahhak ibn Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Ata’, regarding a man who divorced his wife three times and was ignorant, so he married her. He said: : She has complete friendship."
"17525","(17525) Omar bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Ata’, who said: She has a sadaq and a half."
"17526","(17526) Hafs told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Hammad, who said: A sadaq and a half."
"17527","(17527) Zayd ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd, who said: He was asked about someone who married He divorced a woman before he touched her, then it was said to her: She was not forbidden to you, so he consummated the sexual intercourse with her during the first marriage, and she stayed. He was two years old and she bore him children, and he knew by that that it was forbidden to him. He said: He will separate them and give him the wife. From her first marriage, half her dowry, and from his intercourse with her and intercourse with her, a full dowry."
"17528","(17528) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, who said: She has a friendship."
"17529","(17529) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: She has a dowry and a half."
"17530","(17530) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Abd al-Karim, on the authority of Mujahid and Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas That his mother was freed and she chose herself before consummation with her. He said: There is nothing wrong with her, there is nothing agreed upon about him. He will go away. With herself and her money."
"17531","(17531) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan that he used to say: If the slave woman is freed while she is under the slave So she was given a choice, and she chose herself before he consummated the marriage with her, so there is no friendship for her and it is an irrevocable divorce."
"17532","(17532) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, about a man who married his female slave on a specified dowry and then freed her before That her husband should consummate marriage with her, and she should be given a choice, so she should choose herself. He said: The marriage is invalidated and his dowry is returned to the husband."
"17533","(17533) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Mughirā, on the authority of Abraham, who said: If her soul chooses and has been freed Before he consummated the marriage with her, she had no friendship with her."
"17534","(17534) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Abd al-Karim, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Nothing. No"
"17535","(17535) Muhammad bin Sawa’i told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It is not sufficient for her to be compared to him. Until you take it to the authority, you will either be punished or cursed."
"17536","(17536) Muhammad bin Sawa’i told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he tells a lie to himself in the presence of a man, We were in peace and he asked forgiveness from his Lord and would not do that again."
"17537","(17537) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Salem, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: If he accuses her of adultery, if he wishes, he will lie to himself. He was flogged and his wife was returned to him."
"17538","(17538) Ismail bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of al-Sha’bi regarding a man slandering His wife commits adultery and then does not plead with her. He said: He is lying to himself while they are still married."
"17539","(17539) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Ata’ al-Khurasani, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: She is entitled to half of the dowry and not An inheritance for her, and no compensation for her."
"17540","(17540) Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Omar ibn Abd al-Aziz, something similar."
"17541","(17541) Abdou and Muhammad bin Sawa’i narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: She is entitled to half the zakat and not An inheritance for her and no compensation for her."
"17542","(17542) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that he used to say: If he divorced her before he had intercourse with her And he is sick, so she does not inherit from him, nor does he have a share of her share, and she is entitled to half of the dowry."
"17543","(17543) Muhammad bin Sawa’i narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir bin Zayd that he said: She has complete dowry and no An inheritance for her and no compensation for her."
"17544","(17544) Muhammad bin Sawa’i told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, that he used to say this."
"17545","(17545) Muhammad bin Sawa’i narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: She is entitled to the full dowry and to her is the inheritance. And the number is upon her."
"17546","(17546) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Harith, who said: If he divorces his wife three times during his illness, or Before he consummated the marriage with her, there was no inheritance between them."
"17547","(17547) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: If he divorced her before consummating the sexual intercourse with her She has no inheritance."
"17548","(17548) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Saif, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid that he hated to get married. The man is the wife of his mother’s husband. He said: He was a peacock and a peacock, and he saw no harm in him."
"17549","(17549) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: There is no harm for a man to marry his wife’s wife. His mother"
"17550","(17550) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Amr bin Haram, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: Do not crowd with someone who crowded with your father, your mother’s husband."
"17551","(17551) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In the case of a woman who got married and she has a husband, he said: If she brings him and he doubts about him, then it is for the first, but if she brings him and he does not If there is any doubt about it, then it is for the next."
"17552","(17552) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’ regarding a man who divorced his wife and another married her during her waiting period. She has menstruated: the child is for another."
"17553","(17553) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If he kissed her, or touched her, or He looked at her vagina, her daughters were forbidden to him."
"17554","(17554) Gandar told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he kisses the mother, her daughter is not permissible for him. And if he kisses her daughter, her mother is not permissible for him."
"17555","(17555) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who kisses a woman, or touches her, or has intercourse with her other than her private parts. If he wishes, he may marry her, and if He may marry her daughter if he wishes, and if it is a girl, he may marry the mother if he wishes."
"17556","(17556) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of his leaders and Abu Hashim. They said: Concerning a man kissing the mother of his wife. Or her daughter. They said: His wife was forbidden to him."
"17557","(17557) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Abu Malik, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: There is no harm in a slave looking To the poetry of his lady."
"17558","(17558) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that he did not think it was wrong for a woman to give birth. Her dress is in the presence of her slaves, even if he hates him to see her hair."
"17559","(17559) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid and Ata’ that they both disliked the servant to see him. Her lady’s hair"
"17560","(17560) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A woman should cover herself from her servants."
"17561","(17561) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: Do not be deceived. This verse: {Except what your right hands possess} but he only meant female slaves and did not mean male servants by it."
"17562","(17562) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan that he hated for a slave to enter upon his mistress. Without her permission."
"17563","(17563) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak that he hated for the slaves to look at him. His lady’s hair"
"17564","(17564) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that he disliked a man looking badly at his sister or His daughter"
"17565","(17565) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus that he disliked a man looking at his hair. His daughter, or his sister."
"17566","(17566) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, about a man who offers women what is forbidden to him. It is more beloved to me to have sex with women with their heads covered, and if he sees it then there is no problem."
"17567","(17567) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Abu It is valid that Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein used to enter upon their sister Umm Kulthum while she was combing her hair."
"17568","(17568) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In the case of a woman putting her veil on with her brother. He said, “By God, she does not have that.”"
"17569","(17569) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir that he disliked looking at the hair of every person. Muharram."
"17570","(17570) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Muwarriq, that he used to provide intercourse with his mother."
"17571","(17571) Mu’tamar narrated to us, on the authority of his father, that Talq used to make his mother melt."
"17572","(17572) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, that he used to comb his mother."
"17573","(17573) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir that he said: There is no harm in him looking at his mother’s hair. And if you cover yourself, it is dearer to me."
"17574","(17574) Ali told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muzahim ibn Zufar, on the authority of Ad-Dahhak, who said: If I had entered upon my mother, I would have said: Come to her. Old man, cover your head."
"17575","(17575) Abdul Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Hafsa, on the authority of Mundhir, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah that He was making his mother melt."
"17576","(17576) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muzahim, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: If I had entered upon my mother, I would have said: Cover your head."
"17577","(17577) Waki’ and Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Za’ara’, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Being intimate with the man His sister or mother is subject to adultery."
"17578","(17578) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali, who said: Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein did not see their mothers. The believers, and Ibn Abbas believed that their visions were permissible."
"17579","(17579) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, who said: I said to Sa`id bin Jubayr: “Show the man the head of his circumcision?” He said: So he recited On the verse: {And do not display their adornments except to their husbands, or their fathers, or their husbands’ fathers, or their sons, or The sons of her husband, or her brothers, or the sons of her brothers, or the sons of her sisters} verse, and he said: He showed her in them."
"17580","(17580) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, he said: Dawud informed us, on the authority of Al-Sha’biy and Ikrimah regarding this: {And They display their adornments except to their husbands, or their fathers, or their husbands’ fathers.” Until he had finished, they said: The uncle was not mentioned. And the paternal uncle, because they called out their children and said: Do not leave your veil with the paternal uncle and paternal uncle."
"17581","(17581) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sakhr bin Juwayriyah, on the authority of Nafi’, that Ibn Umar was asked about a woman who was permissible. Her maid for her husband, and Ibn Umar said, “I don’t know. Perhaps if this had been in accordance with Umar’s covenant, he would have stoned her. It is not permissible for you.” Female slaves, except for female slaves. If you wish, you can sell her. If you wish, you can free her. If you wish, you can give her away. If you wish, you can marry her to anyone. You want"
"17582","(17582) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Relief is not permissible except with a king, or Marriage, if he is divorced, it is permissible, if he is emancipated, then it is permissible, and if he is granted a gift, then it is permissible."
"17583","(17583) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: I asked him about a woman who made it permissible for her to give birth to her son. He said: No. She is permissible for him except by marriage, marriage, or purchase."
"17584","(17584) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The chastity is not to be disgraced, but if it falls upon her, it is for him."
"17585","(17585) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, a man who said to another: My maid of yours is yours. You may have intercourse with her. She is pregnant, then it is for you, and if she does not bear it, then return it to me. He said: If he has intercourse with her, then it is for him."
"17586","(17586) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, they said: If her comfort is made lawful for him, then it is for him."
"17587","(17587) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibrahim, regarding a woman who made it permissible To a man who was her slave girl and she bore him, and Abraham said: This is a vagina that has come to him in greatness, so he attached a child to him and gave him a child. This is her daughter."
"17588","(17588) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: relief does not He is disgraced."
"17589","(17589) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Khishum narrated to me, saying: Ikrimah asked a man who said: My companion’s mother. She made it permissible for me. He said: It is not permissible for you unless you possess her as a slave."
"17590","(17590) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who speaks to her, he says, “He is considered a friend of hers.”"
"17591","(17591) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: If he conceals his correspondence, then The mother of his son"
"17592","(17592) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Distawai, on the authority of his commanders, regarding a man who had intercourse with him. He said: If he forced her, he is obligated to punish her and punish her, but if she obeyed him, then he is obligated to punish her, but he is not obligated to punish her."
"17593","(17593) Ibn Idris narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Layla used to say: The mukatabite returns and becomes the mother of a child, meaning if He had sexual intercourse with her and she gave birth."
"17594","(17594) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salma, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab in A man writes to his wife and stipulates that he has intercourse with her in his office. He says: There is no problem with him, he has a condition and he To have intercourse with her."
"17595","(17595) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, about a man who had intercourse with him, and he said: He was not pleased Some of it is a dowry when it is freed."
"17596","(17596) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Shu`bi, who said: There is no punishment for an adulterer."
"17597","(17597) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bah, he said: I asked al-Hakam and Hammad about the slave of a man who forced a free woman to be imprisoned. They said: There is no enslavement. Ali, he will not harm you, whether she is a free woman or a mother."
"17598","(17598) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’ and on the authority of a man, on the authority of Al-Zuhri. They said: If A virgin, then the punishment and the punishment, and if she is married, then the punishment."
"17599","(17599) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: No punishment or dowry can be imposed on an adulterer."
"17600","(17600) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If I impose the punishment on him, I will not take it. One of them is barrenness."
"17601","(17601) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Yazid ibn Mu’naq, who said: Ibn Umar said: Because he puts it in my head. I am more beloved to me than having a non-mahram woman kiss my head until it disappears."
"17602","(17602) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is better for him to have lice pierce the brain of a man than for him to be let loose by a woman. It is permissible for him to marry her. He said: And he mentioned that a woman used to have consummated sexual intercourse with a man, so she kissed him."
"17603","(17603) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Ghayath, who said: I heard Al-Hasan say: It is not permissible for a woman to wash a man’s head. There is no mahram between her and him."
"17604","(17604) Abu Usama narrated to us, on the authority of Bashir bin Uqba, who said: Yazeed bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir narrated to me, on the authority of Maqil Ibn Yassar said: For one of you to use a thread and stick it into my head is more beloved to me than for you to wash my head. A woman who is not my mahram."
"17605","(17605) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of his people, he said: I heard his leaders say: I traveled with a woman to Mecca for half a year, and that She was still there and was washing my head or combing my head."
"17606","(17606) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Qays ibn Muslim, on the authority of Tariq ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: I went to a woman from my people and she washed my clothes and combed my hair."
"17607","(17607) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, regarding a man who marries an illiterate woman. He said: He has no right to He brings her out of Egypt."
"17608","(17608) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ata and Makhul, who said: They do not have to use it."
"17609","(17609) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ayyub ibn Musa, on the authority of Ibn Qusayt, that Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab was asked about a man who preached good tidings to With my maidservant, and some of the people said: “He gave it to me,” and Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab said: “The gifted one was not permissible for anyone after the Messenger of God.” May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, even if he had given her a whip, it would be permissible for him."
"17610","(17610) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Zam`iya, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: It is not permissible for anyone to He gives his daughter without any dowry, except to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"17611","(17611) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a man who gave his daughter to a man, and they said: It is only permissible. With friendship"
"17612","(17612) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Ubaid, who said: An alcoholic was asked about a man who marries his sister, or His daughter is the man’s and he should not impose a dowry on her. Makhoul and Al-Zuhri said: The gifted property was not permissible for anyone after the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace."
"17613","(17613) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Whatever woman is, her father will love her. to a man, or if she gives herself to a man, she has a dowry equal to her if he consummates the marriage with her. Otherwise, the maintenance is only upon him if he divorces her before To enter it."
"17614","(17614) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, who said: Ata was asked about a woman who gave herself to a man. He said: It is not possible except with charity."
"17615","(17615) Abdah bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that she said: What A woman was ashamed to give herself to a man until God Almighty revealed: {You may let whomsoever you wish from among them, and may take to you whomever You wish} She said: So I said: Indeed, your Lord will hasten for you in your desire. (Bukhari 5113. Muslim 50)"
"17616","(17616) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, about a woman giving herself to a man, and he said: It is not valid except with charity. This was only for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"17617","(17617) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, regarding someone who married a mahram woman and consummated the marriage with her. He said: No. Friendship"
"17618","(17618) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan that he said: It is hers whatever she took."
"17619","(17619) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, like him."
"17620","(17620) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: There is no friend of hers who entered into her, or did not enter into her, Should a man believe his sister or his mother?"
"17621","(17621) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, about a man who married his breastfeeding sister, but he did not He knew, then he knew after that and said: The marriage is invalid, so if he consummated the sexual intercourse with her, then she is entitled to dowry for what he permitted from her private parts, and if not, he consummated it. Because of this, there was separation between them and there was no friendship."
"17622","(17622) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of the ruling regarding a man who marries his sister, or his wife’s sister. Breastfeeding, so he entered into her without realizing it, saying: She is entitled to the full dowry."
"17623","(17623) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Al-Hasan. He said: She is entitled to the truth for what she did."
"17624","(17624) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, who said: Every intercourse in which punishment is averted includes a complete dowry."
"17625","(17625) Omar bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, about a man who married a woman. So if he fell in love with his breastfeeding sister and he had love for her and he did not feel it, he said: It will separate them and she does not have the right to dowry at all. No part of it."
"17626","(17626) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abraham, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, may God bless him and grant him peace, married her when she was nine years old, and died after her when she was eighteen years old. (Muslim 72. Ahmad 42)"
"17627","(17627) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, that Al-Zubayr married his son when he was young. She took her breath, meaning when she was born."
"17628","(17628) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, that he married a young son of his to Mus’ab."
"17629","(17629) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that Omar proposed to Ali his daughter Umm Kulthum, and Ali said: She is young, so look at her. So he sent her a message and he joked with her. She said: If it were not that he were old, or if it were not You are the Commander of the Believers, so Omar was impressed by your friendship with him, so he proposed to her and married her to her."
"17630","(17630) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, that he used to hate marriage. The two little ones."
"17631","(17631) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, who said: Al-Hasan did not like to marry children."
"17632","(17632) Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, who said: Umar wrote to us: A Bedouin does not marry a migrant, he takes her out of the house of immigration."
"17633","(17633) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan that he disliked marrying an immigrant Bedouin."
"17634","(17634) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi that he hated for a Bedouin to marry a migrant. To bring her out of Egypt."
"17635","(17635) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Al-Rukain, on the authority of his father, who said: Manzoor bin Zaban addressed his uncle. They were Hajj or Umrah, and he said: Yes, if I come back, I will marry you. Then her two brothers, her mother’s son, came out to her. And her father refused, so her cousin married her to her, and he came and she was married, so her father became very angry and said: I am free from this before God. Marriage: I heard Omar say: Bedouin immigrant women should not be married."
"17636","(17436) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Amr ibn Al-Sharid, who said: Ibn Abbas was asked about a man. He has a wife and a concubine, one of them gave birth to a boy, and one of them breastfed his maid. Is it fit for the boy to marry? The slave girl? He said: No, the vaccine is one."
"17637","(17637) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid that he disliked the milk of a stallion and disliked saying Ibrahim is in it."
"17638","(17638) Hushaym and Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that it is his karah, meaning the milk of a stallion."
"17639","(17639) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sabrah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that he hated it."
"17640","(17440) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He used to consider a stallion’s milk to be considered sacred."
"17641","(17641) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Salim that he hated it."
"17642","(17642) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Abbad bin Mansour, who said: I asked Al-Qasim bin Muhammad: I said, “My father’s wife breastfed me.” Is it permissible for me to use the milk of my brothers from my father to show people’s honor? He said: No, your father is her father. And she asked Tawoos, and he said the same thing. She asked Al-Hasan, and he said the same thing. She asked Mujahid, and he said: People disagreed about it, and I do not say anything about it. I asked Ibn Sirin, and he said the same as what Mujahid said."
"17643","(17643) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, who said: I mentioned that to Muhammad ibn Sirin, and he said, “I was informed that some people from the people of They differed about Medina. Some of them disliked it, some of them did not dislike it, and some of them disliked it. We are better than those who disliked it. He did not hate him, but Al-Qasim bin Muhammad was among those who hated him."
"17644","(17644) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, who said: Al-Zuhri came to Medina during the first caliphate with Hisham, and he mentioned that Urwah was narrating, on the authority of Aisha, that Abu Al-Qu’ais came to ask permission for Aisha, and her wife had breastfed them both. His brother refused to give him permission, so Urwah claimed that Aisha had mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Why would you not give him permission? Breastfeeding is as forbidden as childbirth is forbidden. The people of Medina were terrified, so they divorced Abdullah bin Abi Habiba, his servant. Al-Zubayr was his wife at that time."
"17645","(17645) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: He mentioned stallion’s milk, and he said, “Some people disliked it.” Some people made concessions in it, so those who disliked it among the people were better, and Al-Qasim bin Muhammad was among those who disliked it."
"17646","(17646) Malik told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Hisham, that his father disliked the milk of a stallion."
"17647","(17647) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah bin Abdullah bin Zam’a, on the authority of his mother, Zainab Ibn Abi Salamah said: Asmaa breastfed me, and Al-Zubair used to enter on me while I was combing my hair and take the horn from my horns. And he says: Come to me and tell me about my Lord that he is my father and that he has not fathered my brothers. Then when it was the day of the heat, he sent Abdullah bin Al-Zubair He proposed to my daughter Ali Hamza bin Al-Zubayr, Hamza and Musab to Al-Kalbiyya, so she sent to her: “Is she suitable for him?” So he sent to me: You only want to prevent me from your daughter, and I am your brother, and as many names have not been born, they are your brothers, and Al-Zubayr has not given birth to anyone but anyone. Names: You have no brothers, so send and ask, and I sent and asked, and the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, are available. And the mothers of the believers said: Breastfeeding by men does not prohibit anything."
"17648","(17648) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt, who said: I asked Abu Salamah Ibn Abd al-Rahman, Sa`id Ibn al-Musayyab, Ata’, and Sulaiman Ibn Yasar, on the authority of breastfeeding by men, so they said: Do not deprive Something"
"17649","(17649) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, who said: The family of Rafi’ bin Khadij narrated to me that Rafi’ bin Khadij married His daughter is the son of his brother Rifa’a bin Khadij, and she was breastfed by the mother of a son of his, just like the mother of his son whom he married to her."
"17650","(17650) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, that they did not see milk. The stallion is something."
"17651","(17651) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalab, that he did not see anything wrong with stallion’s milk."
"17652","(17652) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, who said: The first I heard about stallion’s milk was while we were in Mecca, so Iyas bin Mu'awiya says: What's wrong with this, and who hates this?"
"17653","(17653) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he did not see anything in the milk of a stallion."
"17654","(17654) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Rashid, on the authority of Makhoul, that he saw no harm in stallion’s milk."
"17655","(17655) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He separated between the two cursers and said, “Your reckoning is with God.” (Bukhari 6854, Abu Dawud 2245)"
"17656","(17656) Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Abbad bin Mansour, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He separated them and decided that she had neither sustenance nor support for him. (Abu Dawud 2250, Tayalisi 2667)"
"17657","(17657) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Omar, who said: The two who curse are separated and never brought together."
"17658","(17658) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Ali and Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah. They said: No. The two cursed ones will never meet again."
"17659","(17659) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Nafi`, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Two people who are in love should not come together. Egypt"
"17660","(17660) Hafs told us: I asked Omar, and he said: Al-Hasan used to separate them, but they would never meet."
"17661","(17661) Jarir narrated to us on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man curses his wife, separate them, and they will not be together. Never"
"17662","(17662) Yazeed told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr ibn Haram, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd, who said: The two do not go together."
"17663","(17663) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: The two do not go together."
"17664","(17644) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The two do not go together."
"17665","(17665) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, who said: Two people who are in love cannot come together."
"17666","(17666) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, who said: The Sunnah has passed that if there is a separation between them, They will never meet again."
"17667","(17667) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Concerning a man who cursed and then lied to himself about the promise. He said: If Cursing, what was between them was cut off."
"17668","(17668) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab regarding Al-Mula’in lies about himself. He said: He is struck while he is engaged."
"17669","(17669) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, who said: If he tells a lie about himself, he will be flogged and punished. The child was returned to him by his wife."
"17670","(17670) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad, that he was asked about the cursed people, and he said: He will marry her if he lies. Himself"
"17671","(17671) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He separated between the two cursers and said: Your reckoning is with God. One of you is a liar, and you have no right against him. So he said: O Messenger of God! So why? He said: You have no money. If you are telling the truth, then it is for what you have permitted of her private parts, and if you are lying, then that is farther for you.\n(Bukhari 5350, Muslim 5)"
"17672","(17672) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr that he separated between the two who curse each other, saying: So he became attached to her. He said: I have no money, so I said: You have no money. He said: So he went to Abu Burda and said: Will all my money and your wife be gone? He said: No. He said: The one whom you commanded to curse between us said: You have nothing to do with it. He said: And he did that? He said: Yes! He said: I came. He said: Abu Burda said: What does this say? He said: I said: What does he say? He said: He says: His wife and his money are gone. He said: I said: What causes immoral people to commit adultery? He marries a woman, then slanders her, then curses her, and takes her money? He said: So he wrote about it to Al-Hajjaj. He said: He said: He spoke the truth. He said: Then a man came to me. He said: I thought that Al-Hajjaj ordered him, so he said: That Did you say something that you said in your opinion, or something that reached you? I said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided it regarding the sister of Banu Al-Ajlan.\n(Bukhari 5349. Muslim 4)"
"17673","(17673) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, that Ali was brought in A woman married a man on the condition that she was bound by dowry and was free of separation and intercourse. Ali said: She disobeyed the Sunnah and handled the matter in a different way. Family, friendship is yours, intercourse and separation are yours, and the Sunnah is yours."
"17674","(17674) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It is not for women to believe men."
"17675","(17675) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Abi Al-Darda’, who said: I asked Al-Sha’bi about a man who married his sister in marriage through him. She thought. He said: She has more right to herself. I said: She is her brother to her father and mother. He said: She has more right to herself than her father if she hates it."
"17676","(17676) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, about a man who married his sister while her father was absent. He said: The matter is up to her father."
"17677","(17677) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Bakr, on the authority of Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’abi, who said: I proposed to a woman, and he said To the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Have you looked at it? I said: No, he said: Then look at her, for it is better that there be peace between you two.\n(Tirmidhi 1087 and Ibn Majah 1865)"
"17678","(17678) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Al-Husayn, on the authority of Waqid bin Abdul Rahman bin Saad bin Muadh, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: If one of you proposes marriage to a woman, then if he is able to find out from her what will invite him to marry her, then he should do so. So I proposed to a slave girl from Banu Salamah, and I was hiding under distress until I saw from her that they were inviting me to her marriage. So I married her."
"17679","(17679) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sulaiman, on the authority of his uncle Sahil ibn Abi Hathama, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Muslim said: I proposed to a woman and I started hiding for her until I looked at her among her palm trees and it was said to him: Will you do this? And you are the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: So I said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: If God places in the heart of one of you, he will propose to a woman. There is no harm in him looking at her. (Tabarani 500)"
"17680","(17680) Abdul Razzaq told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, who said: I wanted to marry a woman, so my father said to me: Go. So he looked at her. He said: So she dressed and prepared herself. When he saw you, he said: Do not go."
"17681","(17681) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in him looking at her before he marries her."
"17682","(17682) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’a, on the authority of Al-Zuhri regarding a man who marries a woman. He said: There is no harm in him seeing To her before he marries her, because God Almighty says: {And if their beauty should please you}"
"17683","(17683) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Sahil bin Muhammad bin Abi Hathama, on the authority of his uncle Suleiman bin Abi Hathama, who said: I saw Muhammad bin Muslimama chasing Nabita bint Al-Dahhak while she was on one of the fire pits of Medina in Basra, so I said: Do you do this? He said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: If God places in a man’s heart a proposal to a woman, then there is no problem. To look at her. (Ibn Hibban 4042)"
"17684","(17684) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: I asked Ubaydah about his saying: “Concerning the orphans of women.” Women to whom you have not been given what was written for them, and you desire to marry them. He said: You desire them."
"17685","(17685) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He said in this regard: You desire us."
"17686","(17686) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, in his saying: {And what is recited to you in The Book is about orphan women to whom you have not been given what was written for them and you wish to marry them. She said: It was revealed about An orphan is with a man and shares his money with him, so he desires to marry her but he hates her. Someone else marries her, then he shares his wealth with her, so he is separated from her, but he does not marry her, nor does he marry her to anyone else. (Bukhari 5131, Muslim 2315)"
"17687","(17687) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Omar, who said: Whoever has her in his room should be left behind. She is flawed, then let him marry her to him, and if she desires him, then let someone else marry her to her."
"17688","(17688) Ubayd Allah narrated to us on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Salamah: {And you desire to marry them} He said: If a woman has lameness or one-eyedness, let them not marry her until they inherit her."
"17689","(17689) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Ammar, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr: {And what is recited to you In the Book, concerning the orphans of women. Neither a woman nor a boy until she has a wet dream."
"17690","(17690) Ubayd Allah narrated to us on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Abu Malik regarding the saying of Allah: {And what is recited to you in The Book is about orphan women to whom you have not been given what was written for them, but you wish to marry them.” He said: It was If a woman is with a guardian who desires her sufficiency or beauty, Abu Bakr becomes suspicious, then marries her and does not leave her. Someone who marries her: {And the weak among the children, and that you deal with orphans with justice} He said: They did not leave any inheritance except the eldest. The biggest one."
"17691","(17691) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of his commanders, on the authority of Al-Hasan that he disliked their slaughtered animals and their women, That means the Sabians."
"17692","(17692) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abu Malik: {So marry as many women as you please} He said: It is not permissible You are among the women, that is more likely that you will not be dependent."
"17693","(17693) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha: {And if you fear that you will not be just in Orphans, marry such women as please you. He says: What I have made lawful for you."
"17694","(17694) Gandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah: {And if you fear that you will not do justice to the orphans} He said: There was a man from Quraysh who had wives and orphans, so he would take his money and tend to the orphans. Then these verses were revealed: {So marry such women as please you}"
"17695","(17695) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Amir, who said: His saying: {And the chaste women are among those who were given the Scripture from Before you} He said: The virtue of Judaism and Christianity is that she washes herself from ritual impurity and guards her private parts."
"17696","(17696) Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: {And chaste women from among those who were given the Book before you} He said: Chastities"
"17697","(17697) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: {God knew that you would remember me} He said: He mentioned it. It is in her soul."
"17698","(17698) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Al-Hasan: {God knew that you would remember them} He said: Concerning the sermons."
"17699","(17699) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar, on the authority of Ismail bin Rafi’, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, he said: I heard him say: The Prophet said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whoever marries a woman and wants to take away her dowry is an adulterer in the eyes of God today. Resurrection"
"17700","(17700) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Malik ibn Mughal, on the authority of Umm Hamadan, on the authority of her paternal aunt, on the authority of Aisha and Umm Salamah, who said: : There is nothing more severe than a woman’s dowry, or the reward of an employee."
"17701","(17701) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: There is no harm in him marrying her for the remainder of his marriage. Her writing"
"17702","(17702) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, on the authority of Huraim, on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: {That is the closest thing. Do not lean. He said: lean."
"17703","(17703) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mufaddal ibn Mihalil, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abu Razin {That is the best thing that you should not depend on} He said: They leaned in."
"17704","It was narrated from Muhammad bin Fudayl, from Yunus, from Mujahid, regarding the verse: \"That is more likely that you will not deviate\" (An-Nisa': 3) — he said: \"That is, you will not incline [to injustice].\""
"17705","(17705) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Qurayh, on the authority of Al-Hasan: {That is more likely that you do not depend.} He said: lean in."
"17706","(17706) Utham bin Ali and Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abu Malik: {That is more likely that you should not depend on it} He said: lean in."
"17707","(17707) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak: {That is more likely that you should not depend.} He said: lean in."
"17708","(17708) Hushaym bin Bashir told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi and Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan. They said: It is permissible Marrying the sick person, buying and selling him."
"17709","(17709) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who was ill and was getting married? He said: It is permissible other than three."
"17710","(17710) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam. He said: Abd al-Rahman Ibn Umm al-Hakam wanted to buy the price of it from The daughter of Jarir, who was ill, but she refused, so he married three more women, while he was ill, so he permitted her."
"17711","(17711) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: Mu’awiyah rewarded him."
"17712","(17712) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zaid Al-Baili, who said: I asked Ata’ about a man who marries while he Is this permissible for a sick person? He said: People say that it is permissible."
"17713","(17713) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who gets married while he is sick, he said: If he was ill, it is not permissible, but if he only married her so that she could take care of him, then he permissible"
"17714","(17714) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abd al-Khaliq, on the authority of Hammad, about a man who marries during his illness. He said: He is one of one third"
"17715","(17715) Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, who said: I asked Ata’ about a sick person getting married? He said: I only saw it as an incident."
"17716","(17716) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Az-Zuhri, regarding a man who marries during his illness. He said: It is not permissible."
"17717","(17717) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Khalifa bin Ghalib, who said: I asked Nafi’ about it, and he said: It is permissible and you inherit it. And take her friendship."
"17718","(17718) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Khalifa bin Ghalib, on the authority of Nafi’, that Ibn Abi Rabi’i got married while he was sick. He wanted her to inherit it, and he and her were related."
"17719","(17719) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, who said: The woman was If she goes to the polytheists, they give her husband the same as her dowry, and if she goes to a people who are not like her And there was a covenant between them from the polytheists {so you were punished} and you took as spoils {so give to those whose wives were taken away an equivalent of what they spent} He says: Give her a pair of sheep like her dowry."
"17720","(17720) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Mujahid like him, or someone like him."
"17721","(17721) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Mukhtar ibn Manih, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Make your choice, so that we may give you sperm. (Ibn Adi 2187)"
"17722","(17722) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, that when Alqamiya married He got married to the nearest house."
"17723","(17723) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidy al-Rabadhi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Kharash, who said: I saw Abu Dharr With the Lord, and with him is a woman who has dark skin, or pale hair. He said: And he is in a black umbrella. He said: So it was said to him: Oh. Abu Dharr, if I were to take a wife, I would be more lofty than this. He said: By God, if I were to take a woman who would give birth to you, I would be more beloved to me than Have you taken a woman who will take care of you?"
"17724","(17724) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab said: What Some of the morals of the pre-Islamic era remained in me, except that I did not care which Muslims I married and which I married."
"17725","(17725) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Alqamiya used to deliver sermons to those below. From him"
"17726","(17726) Yazeed told us: Hisham told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin; That a man married the son of Abdul Khayyat, and she gave birth to a boy with him, but he was separated from him. Shurayh said to him: What indicated to you that He married the daughter of Abd Khayyat, and you were an Arab man with the honor of giving, and he is the one who called on you to be free from him."
"17727","(17727) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ismail, the client of Banu Makhzum, who said: I asked Ata about a woman who said: To her servant: I free you on the condition that you marry me. He said: If only she had begun to free him! He said: I asked Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, and he said the same as what Ata’ said. He said: I asked Mujahid, and he became angry and said: In this A punishment from God and the Sultan."
"17728","(17728) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Muslim, on the authority of Ata’ and Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, who said: He freed him. And do not share it. Mujahid said: In this is a punishment from God and from the Sultan."
"17729","(17729) Al-Dahhak ibn Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, in his saying: {And the souls have brought on miserliness} He said: in Expense"
"17730","(17730) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, who said: Her share is from his soul. And from his wealth"
"17731","(17731) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Al-Nafiq and the days."
"17732","(17732) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid: {Or were you hidden within yourselves?} He said: He mentioned it. In her soul"
"17733","(17733) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Hasan: {Or did you conceal it within yourselves?}: Al-Khatibah."
"17734","(17734) Abd al-Salam bin Harb narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of al-Sha’bi and Hammad that they did not see any harm in giving birth to women. To get married until she becomes pure."
"17735","(17735) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi and Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’ that they said regarding post-mortem women: No. Get married until the bleeding stops."
"17736","(17736) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, who said: Concerning post-partum bleeding: Get married, even if the blood does not stop."
"17737","(17737) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He hated her, so if she gets married, the marriage is permissible."
"17738","(17738) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jalad ibn Ayyub, on the authority of Mu’awiyah ibn Qurayh, on the authority of Aidh ibn Amr, a man from the companions of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was among those who pledged allegiance under the tree. One of his wives was cleansed for twenty nights, so she bathed, then she came and entered with him under his quilt, and he said: Who is this? She said: So-and-so, and he said: Hasn't she died? She said: Then you have seen the quilt. He said: So he struck her with his foot until he pulled her out of the quilt and said: Do not deceive me even from my religion. Forty days will pass."
"17739","(17739) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Al-Aas that he said to his wives: Do not honor me without him. Forty nights during the postpartum period."
"17740","(17740) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yassar, on the authority of Omar, who said: Women in childbirth sit Forty days."
"17741","(17741) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Newborn women wait for forty days and then take a bath. And you pray, and Al-Sha’bi said: Wait for two months, then go to the place where you are experiencing istihaadah."
"17742","(17742) Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Women in childbirth should not sit for more than forty nights, and he said: Atta: She sits as she is accustomed to, and does not sit for more than forty nights."
"17743","(17743) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Awani, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Yusuf ibn Mahak, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Postpartum women sit for about forty days."
"17744","(17744) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhayr, who said: Ali bin Abdul-Ala narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sahl, on the authority of Masa, On the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: Childbirths used to remain during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for forty days, and we used to smear On our faces there is a mask of melasma. (Tirmidhi 1391, Abu Dawud 315)"
"17745","(17745) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abi Yazeed, that he asked Ibn Abbas about a man who bought A maid and a pregnant woman who has intercourse with her? He said: No, and he recited: (And those who are pregnant are most destined to give birth to their burdens)"
"17746","(17746) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: I told him: Abu Musa forbade, when a cover was opened: Not A pregnant woman may have intercourse, and he should not share with the polytheists regarding their children, for water increases in the child, something he said. In his opinion? Or something he narrated, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade on the Day of Awtas that a pregnant woman should have intercourse until she gives birth, or a pregnant woman until she has given birth, or a pregnant woman until she has cleared her throat."
"17747","(17747) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Qalaab, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: He who has intercourse with a pregnant woman is not one of us."
"17748","(17748) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Muqasim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. (Ahmad 1/2561 Tabarani 12090)"
"17749","(17749) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Marzouq, a servant of Tajib, said: We invaded with Rufa’ bin Thabit Al-Ansari towards the West, and we conquered a village called Laha. He tried it and said: Then he stood up to give us a preacher and said: I do not say anything about you except what I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said about us. On the Day of Khaybar, he said: Whoever believes in God and the Last Day should not irrigate anyone else’s crops with his water. (Ahmad 4/108 Tabarani 4483)"
"17750","(17750) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Habib, on the authority of Hanash al-Sana’ani, on the authority of Abi Marzuq, Mawla Tajib, on the authority of Rufayf ibn Thabit, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a similar narration."
"17751","(17751) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace, that a pregnant woman may have intercourse until she gives birth, or a menstruating woman until she is cleansed through her period."
"17752","(17752) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Salah, Qutham, and Najiya bin Ka’b, who said: Whichever man bought A slave woman is pregnant, so he must not have intercourse with her until she has given birth, and if a man buys a slave woman, he must not have sexual intercourse with her until she has menstruated."
"17753","(17753) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: He forbade a man from having intercourse with a man. A newborn, or a woman with someone else’s fetus in her womb."
"17754","(17754) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: When cover was opened, Abu Musa captured captives and wrote to her. The age is that no one should have intercourse with a pregnant woman until she gives birth, and that you should not share with Muslims their children, for water is the completion of childbirth."
"17755","(17755) Muammar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Amr bin Muslim, on the authority of Tawoos, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He was given the command of a caller, so he called out on a campaign and fought against it. That men should not have intercourse with a pregnant woman until she gives birth, nor with a pregnant woman until she has menstruated."
"17756","(17756) Abu Usama narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, who said: Al-Qasim and Makhul narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Imamah, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade on the Day of Khaybar that one should step on ropes until they give way."
"17757","(17757) Zayd ibn Harun told us, saying: Sha’bah informed us, on the authority of Yazid ibn Khumayr, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Darda’, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a beautiful woman. At the door of a tent, or a tent, and he said: Who is this for? They said: To so-and-so. He said: Does he know it? They said: Yes, he said: I was about to curse him with a curse that would enter his grave with him, so how would he use him while he fed him in it? His sight and hearing, how can he inherit it when it is not permissible for him?\n(Muslim 1066. Abu Dawud 2149)"
"17758","(17758) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, that there was a man with an orphan, and she was attending He had food with him. He said: Then his wife was afraid that he would marry her to her. He said: The man went absent, so his wife sought help from his women. And We seized her, and she spoiled her virginity with her own hand, and the man came and made her go away from his table, and he said To his wife: What is the matter with so-and-so who does not prepare my food as she used to? She said: Leave so-and-so behind, and he said: What is the matter with her? He said: So I threw it at her. He said: Then the man started until he entered her, and he said: What is the matter with you? What's the matter with you? He said: So she started crying no more, so he said: Tell me, and I told him. He said: So he went to Ali, may God be pleased with him, and mentioned that. So he sent to his wife the man and the women, and he asked them. He said: They did not confess. He said: So he said to Al-Hasan: Decide on her. Al-Hasan said: I think that the punishment should be imposed on the one who slandered her, and the punishment should be imposed on her, and on those who are to be kept. He said: Then Ali said: If only a camel was given flour. He said: And no camel will grind that day."
"17759","(17759) Hushaym bin Bashir told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that four neighbors gathered, and one of them said: A man. The other said: A woman. The third said: I am the father of the one who claimed to be a woman. The fourth said: I am the father of the one who claimed to be a man. So the one who claimed to be the father of a man proposed to the one who claimed to be the father of a woman. So I married her off, but the one who claimed that she was the husband of the slave girl whom she had married was spoiled, so they disputed with Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan, so he appointed her friends to four women, and he removed the share of her who claimed to be a woman, because she was empowered by herself. He said: So I mentioned that to Abdullah bin Maqil al-Muzani, and he said: If I had been appointed to do that, I would not have seen zakat except on what I ruined it."
"17760","(17760) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, that a woman interceded with her maid. with her finger and said: She committed adultery, so she brought it up to Ali, so the man fined her and beat her eight times for slandering her."
"17761","(17761) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of al-Sha’bi; That there were women in the Levant, so they gestured and made fun of themselves and played with Hezkaa, so one of them rode the other, and the other poked her, So she declared her virginity, so that matter was brought to Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan, and he asked about that Fadhala ibn Ubaid and Qabisa ibn Dhu’ayb, and they said: He is responsible for the blood money, and the share of one person is raised, and Ibn Maqil said: He looks from her sperm to her intercourse, Al-Sha’bi said: And I see that, and she has her own virginity."
"17762","(17762) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Bakr; Two female slaves were in the bathroom, and one of them pushed the other, and her virginity was broken, so Sharih made a ruling for her: upon her. Like her friendship."
"17763","(17763) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he said about two men who married two sisters, so he entered upon them. Each of them has a wife, his companion said to them the dowry, and the spouses return to the one who changed them."
"17764","(17764) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that Ali said that."
"17765","(17765) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan that he also said that."
"17766","(17766) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Khalas, who said: Two brothers married two sisters. So this woman was brought in to this, and this woman to this, so that matter was brought to Ali, and he returned each one one by one. From them to her husband, and he ordered her husband not to approach her until her waiting period was over, and he made for each of them The dowry is on the one who had intercourse with her because he cheated on her, and he made compensation for her, and the fine is on the one who married her off."
"17767","(17767) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Bakr, on the authority of Abu Masoud, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace And he forbade the dowry of a prostitute. (Bukhari 2237, Tirmidhi 1276)"
"17768","(17768) Affan narrated to us, saying: Aban Al-Attar narrated to us, saying: Yahya bin Abi Kathir narrated to me, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Qaridh, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib ibn Yazid, on the authority of Rafi’ ibn Khadij, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The cupper’s earnings are evil. And the wealth of the transgressor is evil. (Muslim 1199. Abu Dawud 3414)"
"17769","(17769) He told us his youth, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Aoun ibn Abi Juhayf, on the authority of his father. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace from earning the dowry of a transgressor. (Ahmad 4/308)"
"17770","(17770) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul-Jabbar bin Abbas, on the authority of Aoun bin Abi Juhayfa, on the authority of his father He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the dowry of a prostitute. (Abu Ali 892. Tabarani 273)"
"17771","(17771) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, in his saying: {And whoever is forced to Indeed, after your compulsion, God is Forgiving and Merciful. He said: Abdullah bin Ubayy ibn Salul used to say to his maidservant: Go. Then we sought something, so God Almighty revealed: {And do not compel your young women to wantonness, if they desire chastity, that you may seek the decency of life. This world and whoever compels it, then indeed, after their compulsion, Allah is Forgiving and Merciful. (Muslim 26)"
"17772","(17772) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They were reluctant to marry Ali. Dirhams and two dirhams are like the dowry of a prostitute."
"17773","(17773) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He forbade the dowry of a transgressor."
"17774","(17774) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, about a man who married a mother and was free in his marriage, he said: He is separated. Between him and the mother, or about a man who married two sisters during his marriage contract, saying: He will separate them."
"17775","(17775) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he marries a free man And his mother in his marriage contract, their marriage was invalidated."
"17776","(17776) Abd al-Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of al-Hasan; Concerning a man who married a woman, then he had consummation with her, then he died, then evidence was established that she was his sister through breastfeeding. He said: Laha. Friendship or inheritance for her."
"17777","(17777) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Rukin; Al-Mughirah, the son of Shu`bah, proposed to a woman, and he was her guardian, and with him were guardians like him, so he ordered some of her guardians to He will marry her to him."
"17778","(17778) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a woman’s guardian wants to marry her with her permission from She was given a man in charge of herself, then he married her with the testimony of a just man."
"17779","(17779) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh that he did not permit marriage with the persecutor."
"17780","(17780) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is no marriage for one who is persecuted."
"17781","(17781) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, saying: He was asked about a man who married a woman, sooner or later, and had intercourse with her, but she claimed that he had not He said: Sa`id told us, on the authority of his leaders, that he used to say: The way out for her is in the urgent, That such-and-such remained upon him, and his entering upon her exonerated him."
"17782","(17782) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Matar, on the authority of Al-Hasan that he used to say: The exit Aliyah"
"17783","(17783) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Humayd, on the authority of Anas, that he had doubts about a son of his, so he ordered that one be prayed for him. The rhyme"
"17784","(17784) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Aslam Al-Manqari, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, who said: Abdul sold Al-Rahman bin Awf is a slave girl who had intercourse with her before he purged her, and it appeared that she was pregnant with the one who bought her. So he disputed with him to Omar, and Omar said, “Did you have intercourse with her?” He said: Yes, he said: So you sold it before you cleared it? He said: Yes. He said: I was not worthy of that. He said: So he called the narrator and they looked at him and joined him. He said: And he was born to him. Many were born from it, but they did not defame it."
"17785","(17785) Al-Dahhak ibn Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of Ata, about a man who doubts about his son. He said: He passed away. Let him join her, for Omar ibn al-Khattab said: Whoever admits that he has afflicted his child, or committed adultery, We will join him to her children, and she asked Ikrimah bin Khalid, and he said: Tell him, let him join him."
"17786","(17786) Zayd bin Harun told us, saying: Sa’id bin Abi Aroub told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Raja’ bin Hawwah, on the authority of Qubaisa bin Dhu’ayb, who said: Omar said: “Grow them well” or “do not give them well.” None of their women will give birth to Ali. In the bed of one of you unless I joined him to it, meaning the concubines."
"17787","(17787) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ammar, on the authority of Abu Muslim, on the authority of Abu Imran, on the authority of Abu Yahya, who said: I saw a man asking Ibn Abbas, and he said: O Abu Abbas, I am a man who tampered with my memory until it was revealed. He said: Ibn Abbas said: Uff, aff. It is better than fornication, and marrying female slaves is better than that."
"17788","(17788) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Issam bin Qadamah, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He is the agent himself."
"17789","(17789) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of a sheikh who said: Ibn Umar was asked about it, meaning Al-Khaddah, He said: That is the one who does it himself."
"17790","(17790) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: He was asked about “those who guard their private parts except from their wives. Or as long as their right hands possess it, they are not to be blamed. So whoever seeks beyond that - it is they who are the transgressors.}: So whoever seeks And after that, he is Aad."
"17791","(17791) Ibn Numayr and Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Huraira said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade al-Shughar, and Ibn Numayr added: al-Shughar is when a man says: Marry me your daughter so that I can marry you to my daughter, or give me your sister in marriage to me so that I can marry you to my sister. (Muslim 61. Ibn Majah 1884)"
"17792","(17792) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar and Ubaidah, on the authority of Ubaidullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, said: The Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade it, on the authority of Al-Shughar (Bukhari 6960, Muslim). 58)"
"17793","(17793) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ma’qil, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a similar story."
"17794","(17794) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafla, who said: They were They hate Al-Shughar and Al-Shughar: A man marries another man on the condition that he marries him without a dowry."
"17795","(17795) Omar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’ in the two quarrels: A marriage contract is to be performed and it is taken for each of them. One of them is a friend."
"17796","(17796) Affan narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, on the authority of the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: There is no doubt in Islam. (Tirmidhi 1123. Abu Dawud 2574)"
"17797","(17797) Omar bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace And he forbade shughar. (Muslim 62. Ahmad 3/339)"
"17798","(17798) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Al Masoudi, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught us the prayer sermon and the Hajj sermon. As for his sermon, the prayer is the tashahhud. As for the pilgrim’s engagement, it is: Praise be to God. We seek His help and forgiveness, and we seek refuge in God from the evils of ourselves. If Allah guides Him, there is no one who can mislead Him, and whoever He leads astray, there is no one who can guide Him. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad His servant and Messenger, then he recites three verses from the Book of God: {Fear God as He should be feared, and do not die except as Muslims} {And fear God by whom you question, and the relatives. Indeed, God is a Watcher over you} {Fear God and speak a word that is just and good for you. your deeds and forgive you your sins} Then you go to meet your need. (Abu Dawud 2111, Ahmad 1/432)"
"17799","(17799) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, that Al-Hussein bin Ali used to marry some of the daughters of Beauty is sweating."
"17800","(17800) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Nasr, on the authority of Ata’ that he recited “In the Name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful” and then married him off."
"17801","(17801) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail, that Masruq married Shurayh but did not propose, then he said: That need has been fulfilled."
"17802","(17802) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, who said: I heard Urwah ibn al-Zubayr saying: She proposed to Ibn Umar to his daughter, and he said: Is Ibn Abi Abdullah worthy of marriage? We praise God and send blessings upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and We have married you in marriage according to what God has commanded: Dismissal with goodness. Abu Bakr bin Hafs: I do not know who said: I think it was Urwah bin Al-Zubair or Ibn Umar. (Bayhaqi 147)"
"17803","(17803) Hafs told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim, on the authority of Hamidah, a servant of Omar bin Abdul Aziz. She said: Omar was He says: Do not let my daughters sleep lying on their backs, for Satan will continue to covet them as long as they do that."
"17804","(17804) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, who said: Ibn Sirin disliked a woman lying down."
"17805","(17805) Ismail Ibn Ali told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a woman converts to Islam and has a husband A Jew, a Christian, or a Magian, and he does not convert to Islam, so she has nothing to do with it unless he enters into it."
"17806","(17806) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is nothing to it."
"17807","(17807) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: They will be separated, and she will have half of the dowry."
"17808","(17808) Harami bin Amara bin Abi Hafsiya told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Haytham, on the authority of Hammad, who said: She gets half. Friendship"
"17809","(17809) Zaid told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr bin Haram, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid; He was asked about a man who was married to a Christian woman and she converted to Islam, but her husband refused to convert to Islam. He said: I think that they should be separated. Between them, if he consummated the marriage with her, she gets the full dowry, but if he did not consummate the marriage with her, she will return to him what he gave her."
"17810","(17810) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, that he said: She is entitled to half the sadaq."
"17811","(17811) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of someone who narrated to him, on the authority of Masruq, that he said: Concerning a man who confessed to his wife. By befriending her during his illness, he said: This is not permissible."
"17812","(17812) Hushaym told us, on the authority of the common people, that it was stolen, and it was permissible to acknowledge it."
"17813","(17813) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is permissible for him to acknowledge it to her. With friends like her."
"17814","(17814) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan that he used to allow that."
"17815","(17815) Hushaym told us, on the authority of some of his companions, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that it was not permissible to acknowledge it because it An heir, and it is not permissible to make a will to an heir."
"17816","(17816) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: The statement is the statement of the man, and Hammad said, and Ibn Dhakwan: Saying what is between her and Mahr like her."
"17817","(17817) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He said: Her statement is what was between her and Sadiq. Her women"
"17818","(17818) Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi. They said: Concerning a man who married a woman, sooner or later, and had intercourse with her. They said: What is clear is that He pushed him to her."
"17819","(17819) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-Shaybani, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, in the mirror you claim to be truthful. After her husband died, he said: He will ask her for clear evidence."
"17820","(17820) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid bin Dinar, on the authority of al-Hakam. He said: She made clear, and Hammad said: : The friendship of her wives."
"17821","(17821) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The clear statement is upon the people of truth, the guardians of women?? And on the family of the man who gets out of that."
"17822","(17822) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Al-Fadhil, on the authority of Ibrahim, about a man slandering He said to his wife before he had intercourse with her: “He will curse her, and she gets half of the dowry, but if she becomes pregnant, she gets the full dowry.”"
"17823","(17823) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Amir, who said: If a man ejaculates with his wife before he has intercourse with her, He cursed her and she got half of the dowry."
"17824","(17824) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Umar who said: If he slandered her before he entered He cursed her, and she got half the dowry."
"17825","(17825) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Zurara ibn Awfa similar to him."
"17826","(17826) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, a similar story."
"17827","(17827) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If a man ejaculates with his wife before she A cursing person will enter with her, and she will have half the dowry."
"17828","(17828) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: If there is a pregnancy, then she gets the full dowry."
"17829","(17829) Abu Bahr narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He will be cursed, and she will have half of the dowry."
"17830","(17830) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was And he made an apportionment among his wives and was just and then said: Oh God, this is what I have divided among my wives, so do not blame me regarding what you possess. You and I do not own it."
"17831","(17831) Zayd bin Harun told us: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabab, on the authority of Abd Allah ibn Zayd, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to make an oath among his wives, and then he would do justice. He says: Oh God, this is my responsibility regarding what I possess, so do not blame me regarding what You possess and I do not possess it. (Ahmad 6/144, Ibn Hibban 4205)"
"17832","(17832) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, that Mu’adh had two wives, and he hated them. That he performs ablution on this day at this time, or that he performs ablution on this day at this time."
"17833","(17833) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Harun bin Ibrahim, who said: I heard Muhammad say regarding the one who has two wives: It is disliked to perform ablution in the house of one of them and not the other."
"17834","(17834) Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Abi Al-Hazm, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd, who said: I had two wives, so I was I am just between them even in the kiss."
"17835","(17835) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: They used to like to Be fair between women, even when it comes to perfume. He perfumes the woman just as he perfumes the woman."
"17836","(17836) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, regarding a man who brings together wives, and he said: If They used to make equality between them until there remained what was not measured in terms of crops and food, and they would divide it, arm by arm. There was something left that could not be measured by him."
"17837","(17837) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fell ill. He said: He made it permissible for his wives to be sick in Aisha’s house. He said: So they made it permissible for him, so he was in Aisha’s house.\n(Bukhari 1988, Muslim 91)"
"17838","(17838) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammam ibn Yahya, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of An-Nadr ibn Anas, on the authority of Bashir ibn Forbidden, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever has two wives, then He will lean toward one of them over the other. He will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection, and one of his two parts will fall. (Tirmidhi 1141, Abu Dawud 2126)"
"17839","(17839) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Ghalib, who said: I asked Al-Hasan, or he was asked about a man who had two wives in a house. He said: They hated intercourse, which is when he steps on one of them while the other sees or hears."
"17840","(17840) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Abu Shaybah, he said: I heard Ikrimah narrating on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He was sleeping between two maids."
"17841","(17841) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’ that he did not see any harm in sleeping. The man between two nations."
"17842","(17842) Hushaym, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ezra, on the authority of Shuraih, that he said about a man to whom his wife was given a gift, but he claimed that he did not He consummated the marriage with her, and she acknowledged that, so he decided for her half of the dowry, and he bound her to the waiting period and said: I do not believe you regarding yourself. And I do not believe you for yourself."
"17843","(17843) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayoub Abi Al-Ala, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He is perfect if If she wants, she can take it, and if she wants, she can leave it."
"17844","(17844) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Omar bin Amir, who said: Al-Shu’abi asked a man, and he said: A man said to the man: When Shawwal has passed I gave you my daughter in marriage. He said: This is not a marriage."
"17845","(17845) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, regarding a slave who marries with the permission of his master. He said: : He is obligated to spend."
"17846","(17846) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A woman should not feel sad with a son, a parent, or a brother except her. With her husband"
"17847","(17847) Waki’ and Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Za’ara’, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Being intimate with the man His mother and sister are part of fornication."
"17848","(17848) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Salman, who said: I do not care if I am alone with my family. And I closed my door and lowered my veil, and I told the people about it, or I did that while the people were watching."
"17849","(17849) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Hamza Al-Amri, who said: Abdul Rahman bin Saad, a servant of my father, narrated to us. Sufyan, he said: I heard Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, among the worst of people is God. On the Day of Resurrection, a man will go to his wife and she will go to her, then he will spread her secret.\n(Muslim 124. Abu Dawud 4837)"
"17850","(17850) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jaririy, on the authority of Abu Nadrah, on the authority of Al-Taffawi, on the authority of Abu Harirah He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Perhaps one of you will tell what he did to his family? Perhaps one of you could tell what her husband was doing to her, so a black woman stood up and said: O Messenger of God, they are... They will do it and they will do it. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Shall I not tell you something like that? The likeness of this is like that of a devil who meets a female devil and falls upon her on the road while the people are watching, and he fulfills his need with her. And the people are watching (Abu Dawud 40151 Ahmad 2/540)"
"17851","(17851) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of the common people, on the authority of Mujahid: {And when they passed by idle talk, they passed by it with honor.} He said: When they came upon Mention of marriage, be aware of it."
"17852","(17852) Hafs told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qays, on the authority of Habib, who said: Omar did not permit marriage in a year, meaning famine"
"17853","(17853) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ubaydah, on the authority of Abraham, who said: If a woman marries his guardian and she does not consent, then She consented, but that marriage is not valid until there is a new marriage."
"17854","(17854) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Omar, who said: If he acknowledges that his children are only one, then he does not have them. To deny it."
"17855","(17855) Hafs told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali, who said: If he acknowledges it, he has no right to deny it."
"17856","(17856) Hafs told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: If he acknowledges it, or is congratulated on it, or says hello to it, then he has no right to it. To be free from it."
"17857","(17857) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi and others, on the authority of Omar, who said: If he affirms The child is the blink of an eye, so he has no right to reject it."
"17858","(17858) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: A man brought a son of his who had acknowledged him, then he wanted to He denied him, so they bore witness that he was born in his house, and they congratulated him and acknowledged him, so Shurayh said: Stick to your son. Amer said: Omar used to decree that."
"17859","(17859) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a man acknowledges his son, he does not have the right to exile him on his behalf. Right now"
"17860","(17860) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah and Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he acknowledges the child, he does not have the right to He denies it, and Hammad said: If he acknowledges the pregnancy, he has no right to deny it. If he wishes, he can say: I made a mistake in the counting."
"17861","(17861) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, who said: If it becomes clear that he is pregnant with his concubine, he has the right to deny it unless he acknowledges it. After she gives birth, and if he acknowledged the pregnancy and then denied it after she gave birth, then he has that right."
"17862","(17862) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Umar ibn Abdul Aziz, who said: If he acknowledges his son Then he denied his commitment."
"17863","(17863) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If a man is estranged from his children, he curses his mother if She was alive, and if she had died, the punishment would be flogged and the child would be attached to her. If it was the son of a concubine, he would become a slave."
"17864","(17864) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad and Al-Hakam, who said: If he acknowledges his son and then denies him, Al-Hakam said: He will be beaten. Hammad said: The boy must confess and curse, and he mentioned that Sufyan used to say that."
"17865","(17865) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Abraham, regarding a man who acknowledges his son and then denies it. From him he said: He will be cursed by the Book of God and the child will be bound by the judgment of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"17866","(17866) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, about a man who acknowledged a child of his from his female slave until he became a man and married him to him. Then he denied it, saying: Denying it has nothing to do with it."
"17867","(17867) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said to him: To exile him, Even if he is a man."
"17868","(17868) Abdou told us, on the authority of Asim, who said: A woman came to Abu Musa, her fathers, her husband, her mother, and her. She is pregnant. Her husband says: She is my maid. I was just playing with her. He spoke to the maid, and she said: My father married me to me. And my mother, and he used to go in on me and do to me what a man does to his wife. He said: So he hit his head with the stone and said:"
"17869","(17869) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and this is the saying of his leaders: {If he is well-groomed} He said: If Their horses are the camels."
"17870","(17870) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He used to recite it: “So when he is chaste,” meaning: “When they get married.”"
"17871","(17871) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: Burairah’s husband was free."
"17872","(17872) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Her husband was free."
"17873","(17873) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Al-Nakha’i, on the authority of Al-Aswad that Aisha I told him: Burairah’s husband was free when she was emancipated."
"17874","(17874) Ali bin Musir and Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Safiyya ibn Abi Ubaid said: Burairah’s husband was a slave."
"17875","(17875) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that Barayra’s husband was a slave."
"17876","(17876) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ikrimah, that Burayra’s husband was a black slave called Mughith, a slave of Banu Al-Mughirah from Banu Makhzum."
"17877","(17877) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sa’id bin Abi Aroub narrated to us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas. He said: He was a black slave of Banu al-Mughirah, called Mughith. It is as if I see him in the streets of Medina. He follows her and her tears run down his beard, pleading with her to choose him, but she did not choose him, meaning Bareera’s husband."
"17878","(17878) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Burayra’s husband was a black slave, it is said He is the one who helps"
"17879","(17879) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha that she freed Bureerah. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave her a choice, and she had a free husband."
"17880","(17880) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha said: Barairah’s husband was a slave."
"17881","(17881) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Khaythamiya, on the authority of Nu’aym bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Omar Al-Awar, on the authority of Abdullah Bin Jafar, he said: Aisha said: Whiteness is half the beauty."
"17882","(17882) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Give it to Yusuf. And his mother is a third of Al-Hassan."
"17883","(17883) Affan told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Give him Yusuf is the best part. (Ahmad 3/148 Hakim 570)"
"17884","(17884) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadrah, on the authority of Al-Taffawi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A man shall not live with another man, nor a woman with another woman, except the father of his child or child. His father\n(Abu Dawud 40151. Ahmad 2/325)"
"17885","(17885) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade He allowed a woman to be intimate with another woman in one garment in order to describe it to her husband. (Bukhari 5240, Abu Dawud 2143)"
"17886","(17886) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, who said: Zayd ibn Aslam informed me, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Saeed Al-Khudri, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A woman should not lead another woman in public. One garment, nor man to man in one garment. (Tirmidhi 2793 and Abu Dawud 4014)"
"17887","(17887) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Masry narrated to me, saying: Ayyash ibn Abbas informed me. Al-Himyari, on the authority of Abu Al-Husayn Al-Hajri Al-Haytham, on the authority of Amir Al-Hajri, who said: I heard Abu Rayhani, the companion of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to forbid us from meeting with him or with him. There is nothing between the woman and the woman, and with her or the man there is nothing between them.\n(Abu Dawud 4046. Ahmad 4/134)"
"17888","(17888) Ahmad bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Shihab, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, who said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade a man to be intimate with a man and a woman with a woman. Ibn Abi Layla said: And I I see in that a punishment. (Hakim 2871, Ahmad 3/348)"
"17889","(17889) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah forbade May God bless him and grant him peace, that a man should live with another man and a woman with another woman. (Ahmad 1/314, Ibn Hibban 5582)"
"17890","(17890) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, that a man asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: May I ask permission to My mother? He said: Yes, would you like to see her naked? (Bayhaqi 97)"
"17891","(17891) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Muslim ibn Nazir, on the authority of Hudhayfah, who said: If you do not do You are about to see something bad about her."
"17892","(17892) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, who said: A man said to Omar: I ask permission to My mother? He said: Yes, ask her permission."
"17893","(17893) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: A man came to him, He said: Should I seek permission from my mother? He said: Yes, as long as you like to see her every now and then."
"17894","(17894) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There was Ata and his sisters in Mecca, in his family and family. In Mecca, one of them would often go to his family at night, and he would come to them at night, so he asked Ibn Abbas: May I ask permission? On them every time you enter? He said: Yes, and he was not given permission to enter them without permission."
"17895","(17895) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Ask permission from your mother, even if She was old."
"17896","(17896) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Huzayl, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: You must Ask permission from your mothers."
"17897","(17897) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Kurdous, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: A man asks permission to On his father, on his mother, on his son, on his brother, on his sister."
"17898","(17898) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of al-Hasan. They said, “He seeks permission for her.”"
"17899","(17899) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu al-Salil, on the authority of a prayer that said: A man seeks permission to visit his mother."
"17900","(17900) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that he said, “He seeks permission from her,” meaning his mother."
"17901","(17901) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, who said: I asked Ikrimah. He said: I said: Should a man ask permission to His mother and his sister? He said: Yes, ask permission for them."
"17902","(17902) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, who said: A man asked Ikrimah Should I ask permission from my mother? He said: Yes, seek permission from your mother."
"17903","(17903) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abu al-Bakhtari, who said: And the woman’s brother. He asks her permission."
"17904","(17904) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abi Yazeed, who heard Ibn Abbas say: He did not Most people are commanded to give permission, and I command this maid of mine to ask permission to come to me."
"17905","(17905) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Satan prevailed upon the people to seek permission during the Hours {those who Your oaths reign over those of you who have not attained the dream."
"17906","(17906) Zaid bin Harun told us, saying: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Muhammad, in his saying: “And those who have not attained the dream.” Among you} He said: Our people used to teach us to greet. He said: When one of us came, he would say: Peace be upon you. Will so-and-so enter?"
"17907","(17907) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman, who said: It was revealed about an-Nisa’: {That those whom your right hands possess may seek your permission}"
"17908","(17908) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Musa ibn Abi Aisha, on the authority of al-Sha`bi: {Let those who Your oaths are possessed. He said: They are not abrogated. I said: For people do not act upon them. He said: It is Allah who seeks help."
"17909","(17909) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hanzali, he said: I heard Al-Qasim and he was asked about permission, and he said: Ask permission at every private sector. Then it is tawaf after that."
"17910","(17910) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his followers: {And do not intend to conclude the marriage contract until the decree is conveyed. His term} He said: The end of the period."
"17911","(17911) Waki’ and Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid: {And do not resolve the marriage contract until The Book has fulfilled its term. He said: The expiration of the period."
"17912","(17912) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Abu Malik: {And do not resolve the marriage contract until... The Book has fulfilled its term. He said: Do not date her during her waiting period. Indeed, I will marry you when your waiting period has ended."
"17913","(17913) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid: {And bury them in their beds} He said: No. Get close to her"
"17914","(17914) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim and Ash-Shu’bi: His saying: {And bury them in their beds} They said: No. He has sex with her."
"17915","(17915) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: {And drag them to your beds} He said: If she obeys him in bed, he has no right to hit her."
"17916","(17916) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ikrimah, and Miqsam: His saying {And drag them into their beds and beat them} He said: Divided: And do not approach her bed, and Ikrimah said: This is the speech, and they said All of them: {And strike them} with a beating that is not painful."
"17917","(17917) Affan told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Al-Hasan: {And beat them} He said: a beating without influential"
"17918","(17918) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Abu Salam Al Fihri, who said: I heard Ali bin Abdullah bin Abbas say: If You had intercourse, so cover yourself."
"17919","(17919) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If If one of you has intercourse, let him cover himself and not be naked like a naked man. (Tabarani 7683, Bazzar 1448)"
"17920","(17920) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Abu Salam Al-Fihri, who said: I heard Ali bin Abdullah bin Abbas say that he was a Muslim. To breastfeed a Christian."
"17921","(17921) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Salih, on the authority of Ghalib Abi al-Dhail, on the authority of Abu Ja`far that he hated to The Jewish and Christian women breastfed the boy and he said: She drinks alcohol."
"17922","(17922) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: He hated for his wife to breastfeed him with milk. Immorality"
"17923","(17923) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abraham, who said: There is no harm in breastfeeding an adulteress or the milk of a Magi."
"17924","(17924) Hushaym told us, saying: Mansour told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Aisha, that she used to say to women: Do not describe me to your wives."
"17925","(17925) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ismail al-Makki, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man marries a mother, it falls Ali and he did not disavow her."
"17926","(17926) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said, “If he marries her, he will not purify her.”"
"17927","(17927) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If he marries a mother, he does not purify her."
"17928","(17928) Ibn Mushir and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, the Messenger of God said, May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: A man should not propose to his brother, nor should he sell to his brother, unless he gives him permission.\n(Muslim 500, Abu Dawud 2074)"
"17929","(17929) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He should not propose to his brother. (Muslim 520, Tirmidhi 1134)"
"17930","(17930) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mudrak, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: He does not commit adultery while he is a believer."
"17931","(17931) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Mudrak, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. (Tayalisi 823. Ahmad 4/352)"
"17932","(17932) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdul Malik bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad, on the authority of Aban Ibn Uthman said: Adulterers will be known by their private parts on the Day of Resurrection."
"17933","(17933) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, who said: The greatest sin that afflicts people is adultery. It is smelly and has no scent, so it is taken and its borders can hardly be fulfilled."
"17934","(17934) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zakaria bin Suhayb, on the authority of Abu Salih, who said: I have been informed that more The sins of the people of Paradise regarding women."
"17935","(17935) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He said to his servants: Whoever among you wants to marry, We will marry him to him. The adulterer among you will not commit adultery except that God will remove the light of faith from him. His heart, if he wants to reject it, he can reject it, and if he wants to prevent it, he can prevent it."
"17936","(17936) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awwam, on the authority of Ali bin Mudrak, on the authority of Abu Zur’i, on the authority of Abu Hariri said: Faith is pure, so whoever commits adultery will be separated from faith, so whoever blames himself and returns to it, faith will return to him."
"17937","(17937) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Asama, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: I have not left behind my nation a trial more harmful to men than women.\n(Bukhari 5096 and Muslim 2097)"
"17938","(17938) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: There is no disbelief in anyone who goes on except those who Before the women, and he is a disbeliever among those who remain before the women."
"17939","(17939) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: The adulterer does not commit adultery when he commits adultery. And he is a believer."
"17940","(17940) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Baja Al-Juhani, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a similar example. (Bukhari 24751 Muslim 100)"
"17941","(17941) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Masry narrated to me, saying: Yazid ibn Abi narrated to me. Habib, on the authority of Bukair bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yassar, that Omar bin Al-Khattab was appointed as a eunuch. He married a woman and did not tell her, so he separated them."
"17942","(17942) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Yusuf, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, that Ali bin Abu Talib used to say: A eunuch should not marry a free Muslim woman."
"17943","(17943) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, who said: I asked Hammad about a man who married off his daughter, then the husband died, and she did not know the son. Therefore, he said: You do not inherit. I asked the arbitrator, and he said: You inherit."
"17944","(17944) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Jubayr, who said: Sa’id bin Jubayr married off his daughter to her husband."
"17945","(17945) Abd bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of a man who narrated to him that a woman asked her son: He married her off, but he thought about that, and he went to Omar and mentioned that to him, and Omar said: Go, and if the next day I will come to you, he said: Then Omar came and spoke to her, but he did not say much, then he took her son by the hand and said to him: Marry her, for by the One in whose hand is Omar’s soul, if only he Hantama bint Hisham, meaning Omar, is the mother of herself. She asked me to marry her to her wife, so the man married his mother to her."
"17946","(17946) Zayd bin Harun told us: Hammad bin Salamah informed us, on the authority of Thabit and Ismail bin Abdullah bin Abu Talhah reported that Abu Talhah proposed to Umm Sulaym, and she said: O Abu Talhah, do you not know that your gods that you worship A tree growing from the ground. An Ethiopian, the son of so-and-so, pulled it out. He said: Yes. She said: Do not be ashamed of that. Convert, for if you convert, you will not I want a friend from you other than him. He said until I look. He said: So he left and then came and said: I bear witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God. She said: O Anas, get up and marry Abu Talhah, so he married her."
"17947","(17947) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, saying: Yazid the grammarian narrated to me, on the authority of Ikrimah; When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would come from his battles, he would kiss Fatima. (Bukhari 3423. Muslim 97)"
"17948","(17948) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Mughal, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Mujahid that Abu Bakr kissed the head of Aisha"
"17949","(17949) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid bin Ayman, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abd al-Rahman bin al-Harith. Bin Hisham, that Khalid bin Al-Walid consulted his sister about something, and she advised him, so he kissed her head. (Tirmidhi 1172, Darami 2782)"
"17950","(17950) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade And he granted permission to enter upon the unseen things."
"17951","(17951) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith and Mus’ar, on the authority of Sa’id bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, he said: He said: Omar: Doesn’t a man have intercourse with a woman unless she is a mahram, even if it is said: her in-laws? Indeed, death protected her."
"17952","(17952) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Ma’abad, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: I heard the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He says: No man should be alone with a woman unless a mahram is with her. (Bukhari 3006 and Muslim 424)"
"17953","(17953) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No. A man spends the night with a woman unless he is married or a mahram. (Muslim 19. Ibn Hibban 5587)"
"17954","(17954) Shababi bin Siwar narrated to us, saying: Laith bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Al-Khair, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Beware of entering upon women. Then a man said: From the Ansar: O Messenger of God, except the father-in-law? He said: The fever is death. (Bukhari 5232. Muslim 21)"
"17955","(17955) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: I heard Dhakwan narrating on the authority of a servant of Amr ibn Al-Aas. He sent him to Ali to ask permission for the names of his son Umays, so he granted him permission, and when he had finished his need, he asked the master, Umar. Regarding that, he said that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us from entering upon women without the permission of their husbands.\n(Tirmidhi 2779. Ahmad 4/203)"
"17956","(17956) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Fayyad, on the authority of Tamim ibn Salamah, who said: Amr ibn al-Aas said: We are forbidden from entering upon unseen women except with the permission of our wives."
"17957","(17957) Zayd bin Harun told us: Hisham told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin that they were not They see harm in a man marrying such-and-such and such-and-such a servant."
"17958","(17958) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm for a man to marry a girl, a servant, or a male. The descriptions and the descriptions."
"17959","(17959) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Abdul Karim Al-Yami, on the authority of Ammar bin Imran, a man of Zayd Allah’s family, on the authority of One of them, on the authority of Aisha, said that she saw her maid and went around with her and said: Perhaps we will hunt the youth of Quraysh with her."
"17960","(17960) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Usama bin Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Sa`d al-Sa`idi that they They passed by a maid who had been decorated. He said: So he called her, looked at her, made her sit in his lap, and wiped her head and called. May she be blessed."
"17961","(17961) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Usama bin Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of some of his sheikhs, he said: Umar said: If any of you wants to He beautifies the maidservant, let him adorn her, and circumambulate her, displaying the provision of God for her."
"17962","(17962) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: Umar said: Do not force your wives to an ugly man. Men, for they love what you love."
"17963","(17963) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he disliked a man getting married on the land of war and leaves his children in it."
"17964","(17964) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Mujahid He hated Christians marrying people of the Romans other than the people of the covenant. He said: Muhammad described a man who was a captive and wanted to He gets married and hates it for him."
"17965","(17965) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: A man is not married to a forbidden person."
"17966","(17966) Ismail bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Abdulaziz bin Ubaidullah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: A man is not married to a forbidden person."
"17967","(17967) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Badil bin Misra, on the authority of Abu Atiyya, on the authority of one of them. She said: I heard Omar forbidding engravings and borders in dye."
"17968","(17968) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, he said: Umma narrated to me, saying: I used to secure brides in Medina, so I asked Aisha, on the authority of the painter, said: There is no harm in it as long as there is no inscription on it."
"17969","(17969) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of a sheikh, that Omar forbade the inscription of ink and tarifi."
"17970","(17970) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hafs, on the authority of Ali bin Murra, who said: I passed by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while I was wearing saffron, and he said to me: O Ali, do you have a wife? So I said: No. He said: So go and wash him, then wash him, then do not come back. He said: So I washed him, then I washed him, then I did not come back.\n(Tirmidhi 2816. Ahmad 4/171)"
"17971","(17971) Mu’tamir and Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rukain, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Hassan, on the authority of his uncle Abdul Rahman bin Haramli, on the authority of Abdullah, the Prophet of God hated the yellow ones, meaning created beings. (Abu Dawud 4219. Abu Ali 5074)"
"17972","(17972) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Suhayb, on the authority of Anas that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He forbade saffron. (Muslim 1463 and Abu Dawud 4176)"
"17973","(17973) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw Sawad bin Amr Confused, he said: Line, line, line, line, line. (Abdul Razzaq 18038)"
"17974","(17974) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Kathir, the client of Ibn Samarra, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Do not approach The angels are surrounded by creatures."
"17975","(17975) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, that when Al-Ash’ari came to Al-Basra, he saw Qays ibn Abbad. And on it was a trace of yellow, or he said: “creature,” he said: so he looked at it, went off, washed it, then came, and Al-Ash’ari said: How quickly he reproached. This"
"17976","(17976) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla that he was called He went to a wedding at night, and he brought yellow oil on it, and in the morning there was yellow oil on his beard, so he washed it, but he did not go and washed it. With soap."
"17977","(17977) Zayd bin Harun told us: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ata’ al-Khurasani, on the authority of Yahya bin Omar, on the authority of Ammar, said: I came from a journey, and my family wiped me with some yellow paper, so I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I greeted him, but he did not respond to me or welcome me. He said: Go and wash this man off of yourself. So I went and washed him, and some of the dirt remained. Something happened to him, so I went to him and greeted him. He did not respond to me or welcome me, so he said: Go and wash this off of yourself. So I went and washed him, then I came and greeted him, and he welcomed me and said: The angels do not approach the funeral of an infidel, nor a person in a state of sexual impurity, nor Imbued with good manners. (Musnad 441)"
"17978","(17978) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, on the authority of al-Nu’man ibn Sa’d, who said: I saw al-Mughirah ibn His branches are covered with creation, as if he were a cripple."
"17979","(17979) Hushaym ibn Abi Sasan told us, on the authority of Aban ibn Kathir al-Nahshali, who said: I saw a man who had wiped His arms had something of a clear appearance."
"17980","(17980) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted and said: The child is for bed. (Bukhari 2421, Muslim 1081)"
"17981","(17981) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abi Yazid, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar, who said: He decided The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took the child to bed. (Ahmad 25. Abu Ali 199)"
"17982","(17982) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id and Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The child is for the bed. (Muslim 1081, Tirmidhi 1157)"
"17983","(17983) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Husayn al-Mu’allim informed us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Grandfather, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: A child is for the bed and for a dark prostitute. It was said: And what is a dark prostitute? He said: The stone.\n(Abu Dawud 2268. Ahmad 2/179)"
"17984","(17984) Ismail bin Ayash narrated to us, on the authority of Sharhabeel bin Muslim, who said: I heard Abu Imamah Al-Bailili saying: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: The child is for the bed. (Tirmidhi 2120 and Abu Dawud 2269)"
"17985","(17985) Zayd bin Harun told us, saying: Mahdi bin Maimun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Yaqoub, on the authority of Al-Hasan Ibn Saad said: Rabah al-Habashi told me, on the authority of Uthman, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decreed that the child should be given to bed."
"17986","(17986) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: A child is for a bed and a stone is for a prostitute. (Bukhari 6750. Ahmad 2/386)"
"17987","(17987) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, saying: Sa’id informed us, on the authority of his commanders, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Ghanam, on the authority of Amr bin Kharijah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The child is for the bed."
"17988","(17988) I narrated on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that He said: The child is for the bed. (Abu Ali 5126. Ibn Hibban 4104)"
"17989","(17989) Abu Usama told us, he said: Shu’abi told me, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a man who enters the enemy’s land. Will you marry his wife? One of them said: No, and the other said: Yes."
"17990","(17990) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, who said: Asim narrated to us, Omar bin Al-Khattab said: You should treat the firstborn of Women, for they are the sweetest of mouths, the healthiest of kinship, and are satisfied with what is easy."
"17991","(17991) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Amr bin Qays, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn Masoud. He said: Marry the virgins, for they are less timid and more friendly."
"17992","(17992) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: You must have gay slave girls, so marry them, for they have the kindest mouths and the most virtuous of morals. wombs (Saeed bin Mansour 514. Abdul Razzaq 19342)"
"17993","(17993) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, asked me. He said: Did you get married, a virgin or a married woman? He said: I said: No, but a Thayb. He said: So let your maid play with her and she play with you.\n(Abu Dawud 2041, Bayhaqi 351)"
"17994","(17994) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qais Al-Abdi, on the authority of Nabih bin Abdullah Al-Anazi, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah said: I walked with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Do you have a woman, Jabir? I said: Yes, and he said: Was she married or a virgin? I said: I married her while she was a married woman. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Why had I not married her to a slave woman who played with her? He said: I said: For him: Ma'ak's father was killed on such-and-such day and left behind a maidservant of his. I did not mind adding a maidservant to them, so I married a woman. You cut off the lice of one of them, and you sew up the armor of one of them when it is pierced, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, you are a blessing. I saw you (Muslim 55. Ahmad 3/358)"
"17995","(17995) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, who said: Omar bin Al-Khattab said: What remains It has some pre-Islamic morals, except that I do not care which Muslims I married or which Muslims I married."
"17996","(17996) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Omar, he forbade a non-Arab to marry an illiterate Arab."
"17997","(17997) Suwayd bin Amr Al-Kalbi told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Abi Salamah, who said: Muhammad bin Abdullah told us Ibn Kathir Ibn Al-Salt said: Our master married an Arab woman, so Omar Ibn Abdul-Aziz was given to him to prepare for him, and he said: By God Indeed, the master of many people has changed his path."
"17998","(17998) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Talha, who said: Omar said: I will prevent the private parts of women of good standing, except among the competent ones."
"17999","(17999) Abu Asama told us, he said: Mis’ar told me, he said: Omar bin Qays told me, on the authority of Amr bin Abi Qurayh. Al-Kindi said: My father proposed to Salman a sister, but he refused and married a servant of his called Buqayra."
"18000","(18000) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Kindi, on the authority of Salman, who said: No. We will not marry them, but we will not marry their wives."
"18001","(18001) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, who said: Ibn Shihab said in Al-Arabi and Al-Mawla: No. They are equal in lineage."
"18002","(18002) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Hassan narrated to us, saying: I asked Ibn Abi Layla about the one who is equal in marriage. He said: About religion and position. He said: I said: About money? He said: No."
"18003","(18003) Abdullah bin Numayr and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: There is no one more jealous than God, and for this reason He forbids immoral acts, whether apparent or hidden.\n(Muslim 33. Bukhari 7403)"
"18004","(18004) Al-Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Warad, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu`ba that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “Are you surprised by someone other than Saad?” By God, I am more jealous than Saad, and God is more jealous than you, and for God’s sake, God has forbidden immoral acts, whatever is apparent from them, and whatever stomach (Bukhari 7416. Muslim 17)"
"18005","(18005) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Al-Hajjaj bin Abi Uthman narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Atik Al-Ansari, on the authority of his father, he said: He said: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Who Ghareah is that which loves God, and among it is that which God hates. As for the jealousy that loves God, it is jealousy in doubt. As for the jealousy that God hates, it is jealousy beyond one’s suspicion. (Ahmad 5/445, Darami 2226)"
"18006","(18006) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, he said: Abdullah said: Lock up the women in prison. Houses, for women are naked, and when a woman leaves her house, Satan looks up to her and says to her: You must not exercise. No one but admires you. (Tirmidhi 1173. Ibn Hibban 5598)"
"18007","(18007) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Harithah bin Mudarib, who said: Omar said: Seek help from women. Regarding nudity, if one of them has many clothes and beautiful adornment, she will like to go out."
"18008","(18008) Abdullah bin Raja’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Sumayyah, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Hisham said: Everything from a woman’s private parts to her fingernails."
"18009","(18009) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abu Jafar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, I am jealous, and Abraham was jealous, and there is no person who is not jealous except one whose heart is inverted."
"18010","(18010) Yahya bin Al-Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir and Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If the curse is warded off, he will be attached to it. The boy"
"18011","(18011) Yahya bin Al-Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, and Ata’ like him."
"18012","(18012) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If there is no curse attached Child by father."
"18013","(18013) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, and Al-Hasan, they said: If he commits adultery A man with a woman does not have the right to marry her daughter or her mother."
"18014","(18014) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If a man has forbidden intercourse with a woman, her daughter is forbidden to her. And when he has intercourse with her daughter, her mother is forbidden to him."
"18015","(18015) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid and a generous man who deceives in front of a woman. They said: : It is not permissible for him to have any of her daughters."
"18016","(18016) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Musabbih, who said: I asked Abraham about a man who committed adultery with his mother and then wanted to He would marry her mother. He said: He would not marry her."
"18017","(18017) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Saif narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Tawoos, that he used to say: If a man marries a woman and divorces her, or if he dies and she has a son, it is permissible for the man’s son to marry her."
"18018","(18018) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Saif narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no problem with him."
"18019","(18019) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Saif narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid; He hated it"
"18020","(18020) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Saif, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Ikrimah, the client of Ibn Abbas; He hated it"
"18021","(18021) Abdullah bin Idris, Waki’, Hafs, and Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Harith. , on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah; {So divorce them after your waiting period} He said: other than intercourse."
"18022","(18022) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: If a man wants to If he divorces his wife, let him divorce her in a state of ritual purity, other than intercourse."
"18023","(18023) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Yazid al-Dalani, on the authority of Abu al-Ala, on the authority of Humaid bin Abd al-Rahman. Al-Himyari said: It was reported to Abu Musa that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, found them ill, so he came to him and mentioned that to him. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: One of you says: I got married, I have been divorced, but that is not the case among Muslims, they divorced. The woman before her waiting period. (Ibn Majah 2017 and Ibn Hibban 4265)"
"18024","(18024) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Al-Hikam. He said: I heard Mujahid speaking on the authority of Ibn Abbas; In this letter: {O Prophet, when you divorce women, divorce them after your waiting period} He said: before their waiting period."
"18025","(18025) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: A man said, meaning Ali, if only the people would The punishment for divorce is as long as a man regrets having intercourse with a woman. He divorces her while she is pregnant and it has become clear that she is pregnant, or if she is pure and has not had intercourse with her since. She is pure, and he waits until, if it is before her waiting period, he divorces her, and if it seems to him that he should take her back, he will take her back, and if it seems to him To clear her way. Leave her way."
"18026","(18026) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin; They both said: Sunnah divorce before the waiting period. He divorces her in a pure state without intercourse, and if there is pregnancy, he divorces her. Whenever he wants"
"18027","(18027) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: I divorced my wife. She was menstruating, so Omar mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Tell him to take her back until she is cleansed, then She menstruates, then she purifies herself, then if he wishes, he divorces her before he has intercourse with her, and if he wishes, he keeps her with her, then it is the waiting period that he said. God\n(Muslim 1094, Malik 53)"
"18028","(18028) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, who said: Ibn Umar divorced his wife while she was menstruating, so Umar came The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told him. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He ordered him to review it, then To divorce her pure without intercourse."
"18029","(18029) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, the client of the family of Talha, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Omar; He divorced his wife while she was menstruating, so Omar mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: He ordered him to take her back. Then he may divorce her whether she is pure or pregnant. (Muslim 5. Abu Dawud 2174)"
"18030","(18030) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: If he divorces her in a state of ritual purity, during which he had intercourse with her, she does not observe the waiting period. This is because of that menstruation."
"18031","(18031) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If he divorces her while he is pure, then He divorced her because of the Sunnah, even if he had intercourse with her."
"18032","(18032) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ikrimah, and Mujahid; (So divorce them after your waiting period) They said: pure without intercourse."
"18033","(18033) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Muhammad; (So divorce them after the waiting period) He said: pure, or pregnant."
"18034","(18034) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ali, who said: No man divorces Sunnah and he regretted it."
"18035","(18035) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Sunnah divorce before purification without intercourse"
"18036","(18036) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Whoever wants divorce The one who is divorce, let him divorce her once, then leave her until she has had three menstrual periods."
